WEBVTT

1
00:00:22.458 --> 00:00:24.458
[icy wind blowing]

2
00:00:38.791 --> 00:00:41.583
[wind picks up]

3
00:00:45.708 --> 00:00:47.458
[water flowing]

4
00:00:54.291 --> 00:00:57.375
[young man] <i>On October 13, 1972,</i>

5
00:00:57.458 --> 00:01:00.875
<i>an Uruguayan plane
crashed in the Andean Mountain Range.</i>

6
00:01:03.333 --> 00:01:05.875
<i>Forty of us passengers
and five crew members</i>

7
00:01:05.958 --> 00:01:07.416
<i>were on board the plane.</i>

8
00:01:10.208 --> 00:01:12.125
<i>Some say it was a tragedy.</i>

9
00:01:14.416 --> 00:01:16.250
<i>Others call it a miracle.</i>

10
00:01:16.333 --> 00:01:18.250
[birds calling in distance]

11
00:01:19.458 --> 00:01:21.125
[young man] <i>What really happened?</i>

12
00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:25.500
<i>What happens when the world abandons you?</i>

13
00:01:27.833 --> 00:01:31.083
<i>When you have no clothes...
and you're freezing?</i>

14
00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:36.125
<i>When you have no food, and you're dying?</i>

15
00:01:37.208 --> 00:01:40.416
[silence falls]

16
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.416
[young man] <i>The answer's in the mountain.</i>

17
00:01:44.458 --> 00:01:46.291
<i>We have to go back to the past</i>

18
00:01:46.833 --> 00:01:49.916
<i>to understand that the past
is what changes the most.</i>

19
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.625
[distant, echoing cheers]

20
00:01:52.708 --> 00:01:54.583
[players grunting]

21
00:01:54.666 --> 00:01:56.416
MONTEVIDEO, URUGUAY
OCTOBER 1972

22
00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:58.166
[captain] Let's go! Get in there!

23
00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:01.791
C'mon, Olds! Yeah! Come on! We got this!

24
00:02:01.875 --> 00:02:03.125
That ball's ours! Push!

25
00:02:03.208 --> 00:02:05.458
[players straining]

26
00:02:05.541 --> 00:02:08.375
- [crowd applauding]
- [woman] Go, Christians!

27
00:02:08.458 --> 00:02:11.958
- [crowd cheering]
- [man] C'mon, Christians! Push!

28
00:02:12.041 --> 00:02:14.500
[player] Get in there! Let's go! Let's go!

29
00:02:14.583 --> 00:02:16.458
[captain] Get it! Come on!

30
00:02:16.541 --> 00:02:18.500
Go, Roberto!

31
00:02:18.583 --> 00:02:21.125
[crowd cheering]

32
00:02:22.333 --> 00:02:23.333
Pass it to Nando!

33
00:02:23.916 --> 00:02:24.916
Roberto, pass it!

34
00:02:26.166 --> 00:02:28.000
- [captain] To Nando!
- [Nando] Come on!

35
00:02:29.958 --> 00:02:32.458
Pass it! Roberto, pass it!

36
00:02:33.375 --> 00:02:34.500
Pass it!

37
00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:36.625
[slams locker]

38
00:02:36.708 --> 00:02:39.875
- [players chatting]
- [showers running]

39
00:02:39.958 --> 00:02:40.958
[Nando] Pass it.

40
00:02:41.041 --> 00:02:42.875
[groans]

41
00:02:42.958 --> 00:02:45.458
There were four players ahead of you.
I couldn't pass.

42
00:02:45.541 --> 00:02:48.559
- You could have, but you thought too much.
- You gotta think less and do more.

43
00:02:48.583 --> 00:02:50.851
- You couldn't have done better.
- Couldn't have done worse.

44
00:02:50.875 --> 00:02:52.958
I messed up once!
We won the last cup because of me.

45
00:02:53.041 --> 00:02:54.125
[Nando] Because of <i>you?</i>

46
00:02:54.208 --> 00:02:56.791
[players jeering and clamoring]

47
00:02:56.875 --> 00:02:58.875
All right, all right! Knock it off!

48
00:02:58.958 --> 00:03:01.208
Hey. What's so funny, huh? Today's score?

49
00:03:01.291 --> 00:03:02.375
[team murmuring]

50
00:03:02.458 --> 00:03:04.333
Roberto, you trust me, right?

51
00:03:04.416 --> 00:03:08.166
So, when I say,
"Pass it," you pass it. Okay?

52
00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:11.416
And when I say the trip money
is due today, I expect it today!

53
00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:15.166
Okay? We have half a plane to fill.
Dan, is your cousin coming?

54
00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.541
- Yeah. It'll be the four of us.
- Our money.

55
00:03:17.625 --> 00:03:19.375
[captain] No envelope? Great, Coco.

56
00:03:19.458 --> 00:03:21.500
- No.
- [captain] Anybody else, then?

57
00:03:21.583 --> 00:03:23.000
Gastón, are your friends in?

58
00:03:23.083 --> 00:03:25.583
- Yeah. I convinced them.
- You're sure?

59
00:03:25.666 --> 00:03:27.750
Yeah, yeah, yeah. Well, except one.

60
00:03:27.833 --> 00:03:30.583
[priest] "'You are my beloved Son, '
He said."

61
00:03:30.666 --> 00:03:34.375
"And at once, the Spirit
drove Jesus out into the desert."

62
00:03:34.458 --> 00:03:38.833
"And He remained in the desert
for 40 days and nights,

63
00:03:38.916 --> 00:03:41.875
being tempted by Satan at all times."

64
00:03:41.958 --> 00:03:43.833
"'If you are the Son of God,

65
00:03:43.916 --> 00:03:47.291
tell these stones
to become bread, ' the tempter said."

66
00:03:47.791 --> 00:03:52.000
"But Jesus answered,
'Man shall not live on bread alone...'"

67
00:03:52.083 --> 00:03:53.333
Psst!

68
00:03:54.041 --> 00:03:55.041
[quietly] Pancho.

69
00:03:56.083 --> 00:03:57.083
Pancho!

70
00:03:57.125 --> 00:03:59.750
[priest]...and gave it
to them, saying, "This is my body..."

71
00:03:59.833 --> 00:04:02.041
[softly] Pancho, for Numa. Numa.

72
00:04:02.125 --> 00:04:06.958
[congregation] We proclaim your death,
O Lord, and profess your resurrection

73
00:04:07.041 --> 00:04:09.291
until you come again, Jesus.

74
00:04:09.375 --> 00:04:12.458
- Come on, Alfredo.
- [church organ playing]

75
00:04:12.541 --> 00:04:14.083
[whispering] Hey! You!

76
00:04:14.166 --> 00:04:16.583
Come here. Come here. Come here.

77
00:04:16.666 --> 00:04:18.708
Hand this paper to Pancho. Right there.

78
00:04:22.541 --> 00:04:23.666
[Alfredo] Thanks.

79
00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.458
[Pancho, quietly] Psst, Numa.

80
00:04:26.541 --> 00:04:28.750
Excuse me. Can you hand this to him?

81
00:04:29.958 --> 00:04:31.041
Gastón.

82
00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:39.750
{\an8}COME TO CHILE, MAN!

83
00:04:39.833 --> 00:04:43.208
[chanting] Workers and students,
hand in hand, we stand!

84
00:04:43.291 --> 00:04:47.333
Workers and students,
hand in hand, we stand!

85
00:04:47.416 --> 00:04:49.208
No, it's the final Commercial Law test.

86
00:04:49.291 --> 00:04:52.000
- I can't go.
- No! It's gonna get postponed anyway.

87
00:04:52.083 --> 00:04:55.083
- For two weeks. Just look outside!
- [Numa] It's not about the test.

88
00:04:55.166 --> 00:04:58.375
- I don't care about rugby.
- [Gastón] Rugby? Rugby's the least of it!

89
00:04:58.458 --> 00:05:02.291
Santiago de Chile, $45.
You'll never find a cheaper ticket.

90
00:05:02.375 --> 00:05:04.625
- [both] Never!
- In your life!

91
00:05:04.708 --> 00:05:05.916
Do you know what this is?

92
00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.333
This little list here has all the numbers
of the girls we've met there.

93
00:05:09.416 --> 00:05:10.291
[Gastón exclaims]

94
00:05:10.375 --> 00:05:12.375
- Graciela...
- Flamboyant.

95
00:05:12.458 --> 00:05:14.250
- Silvia...
- Fine.

96
00:05:14.333 --> 00:05:16.125
- Beatriz...
- A lioness. [chuckles]

97
00:05:16.208 --> 00:05:17.750
- Nélida...
- No, not her.

98
00:05:17.833 --> 00:05:19.458
What? Nélida's amazing. Knock it off.

99
00:05:19.541 --> 00:05:22.625
Nélida messed you up,
left you crying all around Montevideo.

100
00:05:22.708 --> 00:05:25.333
- Whoa! What is wrong with you?
- No, no... [chuckles]

101
00:05:25.416 --> 00:05:27.750
You keep this thing.
Don't let Gastón touch it.

102
00:05:27.833 --> 00:05:31.000
Okay? Let's go grab another drink.
Come on.

103
00:05:31.541 --> 00:05:35.250
- [Alfredo] Stop. What is wrong with you?
- [Gastón] You gotta relax.

104
00:05:35.333 --> 00:05:38.541
Don't let me travel with these two morons.
Please. I beg of you.

105
00:05:38.625 --> 00:05:41.250
[chuckles] You're not gonna convince me,
Pancho.

106
00:05:41.333 --> 00:05:43.625
- Want a good argument to talk you into it?
- Do it.

107
00:05:43.708 --> 00:05:45.083
I really want you to go.

108
00:05:45.958 --> 00:05:49.500
'Cause you graduate in a couple of months,
and you'll start working nonstop.

109
00:05:49.583 --> 00:05:52.958
You'll be the best lawyer in all
of Montevideo, and we'll be proud of you.

110
00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:55.750
But we're gonna have different lives.

111
00:05:55.833 --> 00:05:58.333
This may actually be
the last trip we take together, you know?

112
00:05:59.583 --> 00:06:02.583
[chuckles softly]
You trying to make me cry, man?

113
00:06:02.666 --> 00:06:06.291
[demonstrators] Workers and students,
hand in hand, we stand!

114
00:06:06.375 --> 00:06:07.958
[chanting fades]

115
00:06:08.041 --> 00:06:09.625
[dog 1 barking in distance]

116
00:06:14.458 --> 00:06:16.458
- [bell dings]
- [Numa] Good evening.

117
00:06:19.666 --> 00:06:21.208
[sighs]

118
00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:25.625
- [dog 2 whimpers, barks]
- [whistles]

119
00:06:25.708 --> 00:06:28.583
[playfully] Who's a good boy?
How's it goin', buddy?

120
00:06:28.666 --> 00:06:30.666
- [fire crackling]
- [clock ticking]

121
00:06:37.958 --> 00:06:41.333
- [dog barking in house]
- [indistinct chatter outside]

122
00:07:06.166 --> 00:07:07.041
Champ.

123
00:07:07.125 --> 00:07:09.375
- [Champ whimpers]
- [Numa] What do you think?

124
00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:12.490
- Should we go?
- ["Break It All" by Los Shakers playing]

125
00:07:12.541 --> 00:07:15.708
<i>♪ We want you to come
We want you to hear ♪</i>

126
00:07:16.666 --> 00:07:21.458
<i>♪ We want you to dance
Dance all night long ♪</i>

127
00:07:21.958 --> 00:07:25.000
- [backup alert beeping]
<i>- ♪ But when the music starts... ♪</i>

128
00:07:25.083 --> 00:07:28.708
[radio DJ] <i>It's eight o'clock
this Thursday morning in Montevideo.</i>

129
00:07:28.791 --> 00:07:29.666
[brakes screech]

130
00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:31.208
- [man] Jackass!
- [guys laugh]

131
00:07:31.291 --> 00:07:34.666
<i>This is Berch Rupenian
from</i> Impactos <i>on Independencia Radio.</i>

132
00:07:35.458 --> 00:07:38.125
<i>We're here, kicking off
this four-day long weekend</i>

133
00:07:38.208 --> 00:07:40.958
<i>with a forecast of sunshine
and nice weather</i>

134
00:07:41.041 --> 00:07:43.416
<i>to make your weekend even better.</i>

135
00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:46.041
<i>♪ Now, we know you're fine... ♪</i>

136
00:07:46.125 --> 00:07:47.375
Oh, Panchito.

137
00:07:47.458 --> 00:07:48.458
<i>♪ Oh yeah ♪</i>

138
00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.083
<i>♪ And break it all ♪</i>

139
00:07:50.166 --> 00:07:53.000
<i>♪ You listen to me, break it all ♪</i>

140
00:07:53.083 --> 00:07:56.625
<i>♪ We want you to come
We want you to hear ♪</i>

141
00:07:56.708 --> 00:07:59.291
- Have a good one.
<i>- ♪ We want you to dance... ♪</i>

142
00:07:59.375 --> 00:08:01.333
[indistinct announcement on PA]

143
00:08:04.125 --> 00:08:06.291
Honey, can you help me
find the boys, please?

144
00:08:06.375 --> 00:08:07.958
[Gastón] Numa!

145
00:08:08.041 --> 00:08:10.041
[group laughs]

146
00:08:10.125 --> 00:08:11.541
- Hey.
- [Gastón grunts]

147
00:08:11.625 --> 00:08:12.625
Let's do it.

148
00:08:12.708 --> 00:08:15.125
[captain] Canessa! Roberto Canessa!

149
00:08:15.208 --> 00:08:16.875
Alexis. Alexis Hounié!

150
00:08:16.958 --> 00:08:18.458
Enrique Platero.

151
00:08:18.541 --> 00:08:19.875
Felipe Maquirriain.

152
00:08:19.958 --> 00:08:21.833
Francisco Abal. Pancho.

153
00:08:21.916 --> 00:08:22.791
[man] Bye.

154
00:08:22.875 --> 00:08:24.458
- [boy] Goodbye.
- Okay. Let's go.

155
00:08:24.541 --> 00:08:25.750
[girl 1] Bye-bye.

156
00:08:25.833 --> 00:08:26.708
- Bye.
- Mwah!

157
00:08:26.791 --> 00:08:27.916
- Be good.
- [girl 2] Okay.

158
00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.750
- [woman 1] Okay?
- Kiss Mommy.

159
00:08:29.833 --> 00:08:32.309
- See you! Bye-bye. I love you.
- Love you, Mom. We'll miss you.

160
00:08:32.333 --> 00:08:34.125
- [song fades]
- One. Two.

161
00:08:34.208 --> 00:08:36.250
- [woman 1] Javier, smile.
- [girl] Three.

162
00:08:36.333 --> 00:08:38.666
- [camera shutter clicks]
- [gentle music playing]

163
00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:40.083
- [girl] Done.
- [man 1] Let's go!

164
00:08:40.166 --> 00:08:41.750
- [group cheering]
- Bravo!

165
00:08:41.833 --> 00:08:43.041
[applause]

166
00:08:43.125 --> 00:08:44.250
Did you hear it click?

167
00:08:44.333 --> 00:08:45.583
- Yeah, I got it.
- Perfect.

168
00:08:45.666 --> 00:08:47.416
[excited chatter]

169
00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:48.583
[man 2] Dude!

170
00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:52.208
[Numa] <i>My name is Numa Turcatti.</i>

171
00:08:53.125 --> 00:08:54.916
<i>I'm 24 years old.</i>

172
00:08:55.416 --> 00:08:57.083
It's great that all these guys get to go.

173
00:08:57.166 --> 00:08:59.666
[Numa] <i>I look around,
and I barely know anyone here...</i>

174
00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:05.166
<i>but at the same time,
it all feels familiar.</i>

175
00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:06.958
[laughter]

176
00:09:07.625 --> 00:09:09.541
[Numa] <i>Most of them are young, like me.</i>

177
00:09:10.833 --> 00:09:13.458
<i>Lovingly raised in houses near the sea.</i>

178
00:09:13.541 --> 00:09:14.583
[guys] Hey!

179
00:09:14.666 --> 00:09:16.041
[indistinct chatter]

180
00:09:16.125 --> 00:09:20.541
[Numa] <i>For some of them,
it's their first trip away from home.</i>

181
00:09:20.625 --> 00:09:21.875
[engines humming]

182
00:09:27.791 --> 00:09:29.791
[passengers laughing]

183
00:09:29.875 --> 00:09:32.541
Sit down! Carlitos, stop! Just sit down!

184
00:09:32.625 --> 00:09:34.625
- Come on!
- [enthusiastic chatter]

185
00:09:35.458 --> 00:09:37.218
[man 1] Yeah, you're very talented.
Sit down.

186
00:09:37.291 --> 00:09:38.208
Could be anything.

187
00:09:38.291 --> 00:09:40.041
[guys shouting]

188
00:09:41.666 --> 00:09:43.666
[gentle instrumental music continues]

189
00:09:55.583 --> 00:09:56.958
Coco, look at the camera.

190
00:09:58.833 --> 00:10:00.916
- [camera shutter clicks]
- [man 2] Looks good.

191
00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:04.041
[indistinct chatter]

192
00:10:06.125 --> 00:10:07.958
[man 3] Hey! Hey, Diego! Come on!

193
00:10:08.041 --> 00:10:10.875
[guys chatting and laughing]

194
00:10:10.958 --> 00:10:12.666
Hey. That's a pretty nice hand, man.

195
00:10:14.791 --> 00:10:16.958
- [Carlitos] Dude, your cousin...
- [plane rattles]

196
00:10:17.041 --> 00:10:20.625
<i>Opa</i>! We just got bitten by the shark.

197
00:10:20.708 --> 00:10:22.041
[Gastón] The mountain range, huh?

198
00:10:22.125 --> 00:10:25.083
Is it true these mountains try to suck up
anyone who passes over them?

199
00:10:25.166 --> 00:10:27.333
Yeah. It's true.

200
00:10:28.166 --> 00:10:29.375
[Gastón laughs]

201
00:10:29.458 --> 00:10:31.583
The warm winds
from the plains of Argentina

202
00:10:31.666 --> 00:10:33.583
collide with the cold winds
of the mountains

203
00:10:33.666 --> 00:10:34.875
and create a suction effect.

204
00:10:34.958 --> 00:10:36.416
Nah. You're joking. [chuckles]

205
00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:39.583
[mechanic] I'm not joking.
That's why there's turbulence.

206
00:10:39.666 --> 00:10:42.000
But, you know, we're one step ahead.

207
00:10:42.083 --> 00:10:43.083
Check it out.

208
00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.750
This is the mountain range.

209
00:10:49.416 --> 00:10:52.458
{\an8}And now, we have to go from here.

210
00:10:52.541 --> 00:10:54.416
But the route isn't a straight line.

211
00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:57.666
{\an8}Look. You can't cross it just like that.
The range is massive.

212
00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:02.750
That's why we have to travel south,
looking for a lower passage through it.

213
00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:07.458
{\an8}We cross it, and once in Chile,
we just turn north in Curicó.

214
00:11:07.541 --> 00:11:10.625
And in ten minutes,
we'll be landing in Santiago.

215
00:11:10.708 --> 00:11:13.500
[wind gusting]

216
00:11:13.583 --> 00:11:14.583
[plane creaks]

217
00:11:14.625 --> 00:11:17.333
[pilot] <i>Attention, passengers.
Please fasten your seat belts.</i>

218
00:11:17.416 --> 00:11:21.208
<i>- In a few minutes, we'll be in Santiago.</i>
- Go and deal the cards, okay?

219
00:11:21.291 --> 00:11:23.666
- [guys singing]
- [man 4] Arturo!

220
00:11:25.375 --> 00:11:26.958
[group laughs]

221
00:11:27.041 --> 00:11:29.916
- [clapping]
- [excited chatter]

222
00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.833
[engines whirring]

223
00:11:37.208 --> 00:11:39.375
[wind buffeting plane's wings]

224
00:11:39.958 --> 00:11:44.375
Good afternoon, ladies and gentlemen.
This is your captain, General Carlos Páez.

225
00:11:44.458 --> 00:11:46.791
Everybody, please fasten your seat belts.

226
00:11:46.875 --> 00:11:48.915
Bodies are not allowed
to be scattered in the Andes.

227
00:11:48.958 --> 00:11:50.166
[guys laugh]

228
00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:53.000
Please recommend Casapueblo Airlines
for the forthcoming flights!

229
00:11:53.083 --> 00:11:54.750
[mechanic] Sit down! Sit down!

230
00:11:54.833 --> 00:11:56.416
- [guys laugh]
- [mechanic] Stay there.

231
00:11:56.500 --> 00:11:59.916
- [man 5] Bravo!
- [chanting] Carlitos! Carlitos!

232
00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.416
Stop. Fasten your seat belt, okay?

233
00:12:03.375 --> 00:12:06.291
[hushed] Go to the front.
I need some room to sit down.

234
00:12:06.833 --> 00:12:08.083
Come on.

235
00:12:08.166 --> 00:12:10.166
[excited chatter]

236
00:12:17.708 --> 00:12:20.625
- [turbulence jostles cabin]
- [guys cheer]

237
00:12:23.458 --> 00:12:25.458
[indistinct, nervous chatter]

238
00:12:26.125 --> 00:12:28.458
[woman 2] Sit down. I'll be right there.

239
00:12:30.625 --> 00:12:31.625
[passengers yelp]

240
00:12:32.708 --> 00:12:34.458
[engines straining]

241
00:12:34.541 --> 00:12:36.625
[guys cheer]

242
00:12:36.708 --> 00:12:39.083
Hey! What's the matter? You scared?

243
00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:42.125
[rattling intensifies]

244
00:12:45.458 --> 00:12:47.541
[woman 1] Careful, Javier. Grab my hand.

245
00:12:47.625 --> 00:12:50.500
[girl] Nando. Nando. Your seat belt.

246
00:12:50.583 --> 00:12:52.559
- No! Sit back down. Sit down.
- I gotta get there.

247
00:12:52.583 --> 00:12:54.041
- [groans]
- [passengers scream]

248
00:12:55.791 --> 00:12:57.083
[mechanic moans]

249
00:12:57.166 --> 00:12:59.583
- [screams]
- [Nando's mom] Nando! Nando!

250
00:12:59.666 --> 00:13:01.250
- Susy!
- Don't get up!

251
00:13:01.916 --> 00:13:03.166
[passengers clamoring]

252
00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:05.250
[engines straining]

253
00:13:05.333 --> 00:13:07.333
[woman 3 shrieks]

254
00:13:08.708 --> 00:13:10.708
[icy wind beating against window]

255
00:13:22.916 --> 00:13:24.833
[pilot] More power! Give it power!

256
00:13:24.916 --> 00:13:27.208
[indistinct shouting]

257
00:13:27.291 --> 00:13:30.250
[passengers screaming]

258
00:13:32.333 --> 00:13:33.333
[Numa grunts]

259
00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:35.708
[man 6] No, no!

260
00:13:35.791 --> 00:13:37.791
[engines roaring]

261
00:13:45.416 --> 00:13:48.208
- Our Father, who art in heaven...
- I don't wanna die here!

262
00:13:48.291 --> 00:13:49.708
Hail Mary, full of grace...

263
00:13:49.791 --> 00:13:52.250
- [panting]
- [screaming intensifies]

264
00:13:55.708 --> 00:13:57.791
[high-pitched ringing]

265
00:13:57.875 --> 00:14:00.458
[sounds fade out]

266
00:14:05.250 --> 00:14:07.833
- [explosive roar]
- [passengers screaming]

267
00:14:07.916 --> 00:14:09.416
Gastón!

268
00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:11.333
[wind rushing]

269
00:14:19.166 --> 00:14:20.333
[screams]

270
00:14:28.583 --> 00:14:31.041
[twisting metal screeches]

271
00:14:31.125 --> 00:14:32.458
[screaming]

272
00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:38.250
[bones crack]

273
00:14:38.916 --> 00:14:39.916
[screams]

274
00:14:40.583 --> 00:14:41.791
[Nando groans]

275
00:14:42.375 --> 00:14:43.625
[bones snap]

276
00:14:45.333 --> 00:14:49.333
- [thunderous crash reverberates]
- [silence falls]

277
00:14:52.250 --> 00:14:54.791
[ominous, low droning resonates]

278
00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:00.916
[muffled, metallic creaking]

279
00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:25.416
[buckle clicks, echoes]

280
00:15:26.416 --> 00:15:28.916
[passengers crying out]

281
00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:31.375
[sounds distort]

282
00:15:36.208 --> 00:15:37.625
[distortion subsides]

283
00:15:42.166 --> 00:15:44.000
[man 1] Give me your hand, Roberto.

284
00:15:45.375 --> 00:15:47.208
[metal creaks]

285
00:15:47.291 --> 00:15:49.250
- [shivering]
- [man 2] I'm down here!

286
00:15:49.333 --> 00:15:50.708
[panicked shouts]

287
00:15:50.791 --> 00:15:52.708
Eduardo. Eduardo. Eduardo.

288
00:15:52.791 --> 00:15:54.166
- Shh.
- Marcelo.

289
00:15:55.208 --> 00:15:57.583
Yeah, man. Yeah. I'm right here. I'm here.

290
00:15:57.666 --> 00:16:01.458
[groaning weakly]

291
00:16:01.541 --> 00:16:04.625
[man 3, echoing] I don't want
anyone else to die!

292
00:16:04.708 --> 00:16:09.000
I don't want anyone else to die!
I don't want anyone else to die!

293
00:16:09.708 --> 00:16:12.541
[Roberto] Put him against the wall.
Okay, that's great. Lift him up.

294
00:16:12.625 --> 00:16:14.333
[breathing shakily]

295
00:16:14.416 --> 00:16:17.041
That's it. I need you to be calm.
Relax, relax. Now, breathe.

296
00:16:17.125 --> 00:16:20.458
Look into my eyes.
Look into my eyes. I study medicine.

297
00:16:20.541 --> 00:16:22.333
I'm Roberto. What's your name?

298
00:16:22.416 --> 00:16:23.833
- Álvaro.
- Álvaro what?

299
00:16:23.916 --> 00:16:26.041
- Álvaro... Álvaro... [screams]
- [bones snap]

300
00:16:26.125 --> 00:16:28.791
[sounds distort, fade]

301
00:16:32.875 --> 00:16:34.666
[passengers screaming]

302
00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:36.666
- [fuselage groans]
- [man 4] Please wake up!

303
00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:39.041
[man 5] The pilot's alive! Here, help me.

304
00:16:39.125 --> 00:16:40.500
The pilot is alive!

305
00:16:40.583 --> 00:16:41.916
Come on, Gustavo.

306
00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:45.625
- On three, okay? One, two, three.
- [group grunts]

307
00:16:45.708 --> 00:16:46.958
[man 1] This way. Here.

308
00:16:47.041 --> 00:16:48.458
DAY 1
OCTOBER 13, 1972

309
00:16:49.625 --> 00:16:51.291
- [man 1] Right here.
- [glass crunches]

310
00:16:51.375 --> 00:16:52.916
[group grunts]

311
00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:56.041
Nothing's turning on. Not even the lights.

312
00:16:56.125 --> 00:16:58.416
I need you to tell me how the radio works.

313
00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:00.416
- What? What do I press?
- [splutters]

314
00:17:01.625 --> 00:17:03.166
[panting]

315
00:17:04.041 --> 00:17:07.291
Hello? We crashed in the mountains.
We're Uruguayans.

316
00:17:07.375 --> 00:17:09.750
We crashed in the mountains.
Is anybody there?

317
00:17:10.375 --> 00:17:11.458
Does this even work?

318
00:17:11.541 --> 00:17:14.708
- Huh? What?
- [weakly] We passed Curicó.

319
00:17:15.208 --> 00:17:16.208
What do you mean?

320
00:17:16.291 --> 00:17:17.833
We're past Curicó.

321
00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:20.250
What about Curicó?

322
00:17:20.333 --> 00:17:22.458
- Say it again. Come on.
- [pilot wheezing]

323
00:17:22.541 --> 00:17:24.125
- [coughs]
- [man 2] Hey!

324
00:17:24.208 --> 00:17:25.875
[passengers shouting in fuselage]

325
00:17:28.916 --> 00:17:30.916
[pilot gasping for air]

326
00:17:33.916 --> 00:17:35.791
[spluttering, murmuring]

327
00:17:38.875 --> 00:17:40.875
[choking gasps]

328
00:17:46.708 --> 00:17:48.833
[straining] May... may God be with you.

329
00:17:51.708 --> 00:17:52.708
[coughs weakly]

330
00:17:52.791 --> 00:17:56.250
- [wind whistling]
- [somber string music playing]

331
00:17:59.375 --> 00:18:01.583
[Numa] <i>The night hits like an ambush.</i>

332
00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:07.541
<i>In the span of minutes,
temperature drops 86 degrees.</i>

333
00:18:09.208 --> 00:18:11.916
<i>If the plane crash didn't kill us,
the cold will.</i>

334
00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:14.000
[cries of pain and panic]

335
00:18:16.166 --> 00:18:17.583
[passengers shivering]

336
00:18:17.666 --> 00:18:19.791
[Numa] <i>We huddle together the best we can.</i>

337
00:18:20.875 --> 00:18:23.666
<i>Living and dead... as one.</i>

338
00:18:24.166 --> 00:18:26.166
[wind knocking against fuselage]

339
00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:27.666
[man 1 screams]

340
00:18:28.166 --> 00:18:29.375
[bottle cracks]

341
00:18:29.458 --> 00:18:31.541
[Numa breathing heavily]

342
00:18:33.458 --> 00:18:35.166
[screams]

343
00:18:35.750 --> 00:18:38.375
- [moans]
- [takes a breath] I'm going home now.

344
00:18:38.458 --> 00:18:41.541
Your passport! Give me your passport!
Your passport!

345
00:18:42.333 --> 00:18:43.875
Grab my hand tighter.

346
00:18:44.875 --> 00:18:46.625
[Numa] <i>That's how we spend the night.</i>

347
00:18:46.708 --> 00:18:48.958
Nobody fall asleep!
You'll freeze to death!

348
00:18:49.041 --> 00:18:51.458
- [Numa] <i>The injured scream.</i>
- [Marcelo] Come on!

349
00:18:51.541 --> 00:18:53.500
[Numa] <i>So do the rest of us.</i>

350
00:18:53.583 --> 00:18:56.041
Let go of me! Mommy!

351
00:18:56.666 --> 00:18:58.208
[crying] Mommy!

352
00:18:58.291 --> 00:18:59.166
Hold me.

353
00:18:59.250 --> 00:19:01.250
[somber string music building]

354
00:19:03.875 --> 00:19:05.416
Tighter, Pancho.

355
00:19:08.625 --> 00:19:10.083
[Abal coughs]

356
00:19:10.166 --> 00:19:12.625
[shakily] Help me. Help me.

357
00:19:12.708 --> 00:19:14.875
[spluttering] Help.

358
00:19:14.958 --> 00:19:16.625
[shivering] Help!

359
00:19:16.708 --> 00:19:18.666
[silence falls]

360
00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:20.750
[wind whistling outside]

361
00:19:26.416 --> 00:19:29.250
[Numa breathing shakily]

362
00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:33.500
[survivors shivering]

363
00:19:58.125 --> 00:19:59.416
[Numa sighs, relieved]

364
00:20:01.083 --> 00:20:04.291
We're still alive, Pancho. [laughs]

365
00:20:08.333 --> 00:20:11.041
[rattling reverberates across valley]

366
00:20:13.708 --> 00:20:15.708
[breathing heavily]

367
00:20:15.791 --> 00:20:17.791
[snow crunching underfoot]

368
00:20:20.666 --> 00:20:23.666
[ominous music playing]

369
00:20:40.041 --> 00:20:42.000
[panting]

370
00:20:47.291 --> 00:20:49.291
[breathing shakily]

371
00:20:57.416 --> 00:20:59.416
[both shivering]

372
00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:08.166
You got another one?

373
00:21:11.666 --> 00:21:12.791
Do we know where we are?

374
00:21:14.083 --> 00:21:15.166
No, not yet.

375
00:21:15.666 --> 00:21:18.833
Marcelo. We lost three more.
Pancho Abal and Martínez Lamas.

376
00:21:18.916 --> 00:21:20.791
And the lady who was screaming.

377
00:21:21.916 --> 00:21:24.333
Gastón got sucked out
when the tail broke off.

378
00:21:25.041 --> 00:21:29.208
Also, my cousin Daniel
and Guido and Alexis.

379
00:21:29.291 --> 00:21:30.333
[music fades]

380
00:21:30.416 --> 00:21:31.625
Nando may not make it.

381
00:21:32.916 --> 00:21:34.291
His sister's really weak.

382
00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:37.000
We don't have anywhere
to take care of the injured.

383
00:21:37.083 --> 00:21:39.750
[sighs] Let's make room inside the plane.

384
00:21:40.916 --> 00:21:43.875
<i>Let's take out the seats
so we can all fit in there.</i>

385
00:21:46.041 --> 00:21:47.750
[both grunting]

386
00:21:47.833 --> 00:21:50.000
[somber instrumental music playing]

387
00:21:50.083 --> 00:21:51.083
C'mon, guys. C'mon.

388
00:21:51.166 --> 00:21:52.750
[group panting]

389
00:21:52.833 --> 00:21:54.708
[Marcelo] <i>We need
to prioritize the injured.</i>

390
00:21:54.791 --> 00:21:58.000
So let's clean up this side of the plane.
That's where the sun is.

391
00:21:58.083 --> 00:22:01.916
<i>We'll take anyone who's hurt over there
and help them as much as we can.</i>

392
00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:05.559
- [Marcelo] <i>Platero!
- Yeah?</i>

393
00:22:05.583 --> 00:22:09.000
Anything you find that might be useful,
put in a suitcase. Okay?

394
00:22:09.083 --> 00:22:10.958
See if you can find
any food in the luggage.

395
00:22:11.625 --> 00:22:14.333
<i>Anything you find,
put in a single suitcase.</i>

396
00:22:22.291 --> 00:22:23.666
[man] Bobby. Bobby.

397
00:22:23.750 --> 00:22:25.208
What do we do with the dead?

398
00:22:26.166 --> 00:22:29.416
We put them over there, on that side.

399
00:22:29.500 --> 00:22:30.916
<i>Until rescue comes.</i>

400
00:22:33.208 --> 00:22:35.541
[group panting]

401
00:22:35.625 --> 00:22:37.625
[somber music building]

402
00:22:44.708 --> 00:22:48.750
EUGENIA DOLGAY DE PARRADO - AGE 50
GRAZIELA GUMILA DE MARIANI - AGE 43

403
00:22:48.833 --> 00:22:50.750
DANTE LAGURARA - AGE 41

404
00:22:50.833 --> 00:22:54.791
ESTHER HORTA DE NICOLA - AGE 40
FRANCISCO NICOLA - AGE 40

405
00:22:54.875 --> 00:22:58.791
JULIO FERRADÁS - AGE 39
JULIO MARTÍNEZ LAMAS - AGE 24

406
00:22:58.875 --> 00:23:02.875
FELIPE MAQUIRRIAIN - AGE 22
FRANCISCO "PANCHO" ABAL - AGE 21

407
00:23:02.958 --> 00:23:09.708
FERNANDO VÁZQUEZ - AGE 20
CARLOS VALETA - AGE 18

408
00:23:09.791 --> 00:23:12.833
[somber music fades]

409
00:23:12.916 --> 00:23:14.916
[wind gusting]

410
00:23:29.708 --> 00:23:31.375
[Marcelo] Here, take one, okay?

411
00:23:31.458 --> 00:23:32.666
We gotta make it last.

412
00:23:32.750 --> 00:23:34.208
[indistinct chatter]

413
00:23:40.541 --> 00:23:42.541
[engine whirring in distance]

414
00:23:50.625 --> 00:23:52.000
Hey!

415
00:23:53.166 --> 00:23:55.000
Hey!

416
00:23:55.083 --> 00:23:57.000
Help!

417
00:23:57.083 --> 00:23:59.458
- Help!
- [man] Hey!

418
00:23:59.541 --> 00:24:01.500
- [whirring fades]
- Over here! [echoing]

419
00:24:02.166 --> 00:24:08.083
DAY 2
OCTOBER 14, 1972

420
00:24:08.916 --> 00:24:11.833
- [man 1] Wait. Stop.
- [Carlitos] No. Isn't there a bigger one?

421
00:24:11.916 --> 00:24:14.583
- That one there. Roy!
- [man 2] No! Don't touch it.

422
00:24:14.666 --> 00:24:17.291
[Carlitos] See if you can find rags,
coats, clothes.

423
00:24:17.375 --> 00:24:18.541
[guys strain]

424
00:24:18.625 --> 00:24:20.458
[Roy] Here. Take it.

425
00:24:20.541 --> 00:24:22.125
- [exhales]
- [Roy] Come on.

426
00:24:22.208 --> 00:24:24.934
- [Carlitos] Look for fabric, clothes...
- [Marcelo] Give me that one.

427
00:24:24.958 --> 00:24:28.083
[Roy] Coco! Take this. It's bigger.

428
00:24:28.166 --> 00:24:29.541
How many are gonna die tonight?

429
00:24:30.666 --> 00:24:32.291
No one's gonna die, Carlitos.

430
00:24:32.958 --> 00:24:34.208
I promise.

431
00:24:34.291 --> 00:24:36.125
- [Roy] Pancho! More bags!
- [wind picks up]

432
00:24:40.833 --> 00:24:43.708
Here, cover all those holes
so that the cold doesn't get in at night.

433
00:24:44.625 --> 00:24:46.625
[footsteps approaching]

434
00:24:49.416 --> 00:24:51.333
[Marcelo shivering]

435
00:24:55.250 --> 00:24:56.625
[quietly] Marcelo.

436
00:25:01.291 --> 00:25:03.291
[indistinct chatter inside cabin]

437
00:25:07.041 --> 00:25:08.291
They're coming.

438
00:25:12.666 --> 00:25:13.833
Tomorrow.

439
00:25:16.041 --> 00:25:17.208
[sighs]

440
00:25:17.291 --> 00:25:18.750
[wind picks up]

441
00:25:20.791 --> 00:25:23.666
[Numa] <i>Fito Strauch
isn't as optimistic as Marcelo.</i>

442
00:25:24.458 --> 00:25:25.833
<i>He's a reasonable man.</i>

443
00:25:26.708 --> 00:25:28.791
<i>He would never go against the captain.</i>

444
00:25:31.041 --> 00:25:33.083
<i>But he doesn't like what he sees.</i>

445
00:25:36.291 --> 00:25:39.083
<i>This is a place where life is impossible.</i>

446
00:25:42.833 --> 00:25:45.083
<i>Out here, we are an anomaly.</i>

447
00:25:48.375 --> 00:25:55.291
{\an8}DAY 3
OCTOBER 15, 1972

448
00:25:55.375 --> 00:25:56.875
{\an8}[metal creaking in distance]

449
00:25:56.958 --> 00:26:00.500
- [labored breathing]
- [Roberto] Nando. Nando.

450
00:26:06.500 --> 00:26:08.416
No. No. Uh, Nando... Don't.

451
00:26:08.916 --> 00:26:11.708
[grunts] Shit.

452
00:26:11.791 --> 00:26:13.708
- Here. Take it.
- Give me that. Thanks.

453
00:26:16.791 --> 00:26:19.083
- [Nando mumbles, sighs]
- I can't hear you.

454
00:26:20.791 --> 00:26:22.041
What happened?

455
00:26:23.541 --> 00:26:24.750
Plane crashed.

456
00:26:26.500 --> 00:26:27.500
[Nando] My sister?

457
00:26:28.833 --> 00:26:29.833
Susy?

458
00:26:30.291 --> 00:26:32.041
Susy's over there, resting.

459
00:26:32.125 --> 00:26:33.708
[Nando grunting]

460
00:26:45.208 --> 00:26:47.125
[Susy groaning weakly]

461
00:26:53.666 --> 00:26:54.958
[quietly] Where's my mom?

462
00:26:57.125 --> 00:26:58.666
[Roberto] Your mom died, Nando.

463
00:27:04.708 --> 00:27:07.125
[speaking inaudibly]

464
00:27:07.208 --> 00:27:09.833
[gentle music playing]

465
00:27:11.458 --> 00:27:12.625
[present-day Nando gasps]

466
00:27:12.708 --> 00:27:15.208
- [Nando] Bye, Dad.
- See you Monday. Take care of them.

467
00:27:15.291 --> 00:27:16.291
Yeah, yeah.

468
00:27:17.416 --> 00:27:18.500
I got it.

469
00:27:19.541 --> 00:27:21.541
[Nando breathing shakily]

470
00:27:27.666 --> 00:27:30.625
- [Nando] How long have we been here?
- Three days.

471
00:27:37.583 --> 00:27:38.708
They seen us?

472
00:27:51.666 --> 00:27:52.833
[music fades]

473
00:27:52.916 --> 00:27:54.000
[grunts]

474
00:27:54.083 --> 00:27:56.083
[panting]

475
00:28:01.708 --> 00:28:03.041
[water trickling]

476
00:28:06.375 --> 00:28:08.375
[group breathing heavily]

477
00:28:13.458 --> 00:28:15.375
[Marcelo] Give me that. Okay. Thanks.

478
00:28:15.875 --> 00:28:17.875
[plane engines whirring in distance]

479
00:28:23.250 --> 00:28:25.250
[hum of engines echoes across valley]

480
00:28:25.333 --> 00:28:28.375
[survivors shouting and whistling below]

481
00:28:33.458 --> 00:28:35.333
Hey!

482
00:28:35.416 --> 00:28:37.833
- Over here!
- Hey! It rocked its wings! They saw us!

483
00:28:37.916 --> 00:28:39.541
- They saw us!
- The wings moved!

484
00:28:39.625 --> 00:28:41.291
- [group cheers]
- [sobs]

485
00:28:41.375 --> 00:28:42.708
- [man] Over here!
- Whoo-hoo!

486
00:28:42.791 --> 00:28:44.500
[whirring fades]

487
00:28:45.708 --> 00:28:49.916
- [all shouting and cheering]
- [crying]

488
00:28:50.000 --> 00:28:52.000
[anxious silence falls]

489
00:28:54.375 --> 00:28:55.375
[sighs]

490
00:28:59.666 --> 00:29:01.375
[Coco] Do you know what I'd love to eat?

491
00:29:02.375 --> 00:29:04.625
A chivito from Arocena's.

492
00:29:04.708 --> 00:29:06.333
A full-stuffed Canadian chivito?

493
00:29:06.416 --> 00:29:08.416
[inhales] A milanesa from La Mascota.

494
00:29:08.500 --> 00:29:11.750
- [man 1] Oh yeah. That'd be great.
- Oh. Fries on the side.

495
00:29:11.833 --> 00:29:14.500
- I love their milanesas. So good.
- They're the best.

496
00:29:14.583 --> 00:29:17.500
Incredible. And the size
of the milanesas of La Mascota.

497
00:29:17.583 --> 00:29:20.958
- [man 2] Fries... and ham. Bacon.
- Hey.

498
00:29:21.041 --> 00:29:22.583
[man 3 coughs]

499
00:29:24.000 --> 00:29:26.166
They could've dropped
some food from the plane, right?

500
00:29:27.541 --> 00:29:29.125
[sighs] Well, that wouldn't make sense.

501
00:29:30.541 --> 00:29:33.250
If they drop a package like that,
it'd sink in the snow.

502
00:29:33.333 --> 00:29:34.875
We'd never get it.

503
00:29:39.208 --> 00:29:40.750
[metal rattles]

504
00:29:42.916 --> 00:29:44.833
[seat belts strain]

505
00:29:49.208 --> 00:29:50.625
[Roberto] Bring in the injured.

506
00:29:50.708 --> 00:29:52.625
- [groaning]
- [Roberto] Easy. Easy. Okay.

507
00:29:52.708 --> 00:29:54.458
Careful with his legs. Right there.

508
00:29:54.541 --> 00:29:58.416
- You'll be better there, Arturo. Easy.
- [grunts, panting]

509
00:30:00.541 --> 00:30:03.958
[plane engines whirring in distance]

510
00:30:07.750 --> 00:30:09.809
- [survivors murmuring]
- [man 1] It's getting closer.

511
00:30:09.833 --> 00:30:13.291
- [whirring echoes across valley]
- [man 2] I don't see anything.

512
00:30:13.375 --> 00:30:15.791
- [man 3] Yeah. Me neither.
- [man 4] You see something?

513
00:30:15.875 --> 00:30:17.083
[man 1] I don't see it.

514
00:30:24.041 --> 00:30:26.041
[whirring fades]

515
00:30:26.125 --> 00:30:28.833
[wind gusting]

516
00:30:28.916 --> 00:30:29.958
[Numa sighs]

517
00:30:34.250 --> 00:30:35.875
[Daniel] The Andes are massive.

518
00:30:36.833 --> 00:30:39.541
They must be organizing
the search somehow.

519
00:30:39.625 --> 00:30:40.958
By zone.

520
00:30:41.041 --> 00:30:42.791
Yesterday, they were here.

521
00:30:42.875 --> 00:30:44.375
We saw them fly over.

522
00:30:45.291 --> 00:30:47.125
We heard them today,
but we couldn't see them.

523
00:30:47.208 --> 00:30:49.083
They're probably searching somewhere else.

524
00:30:49.166 --> 00:30:50.726
If they're looking, they didn't see us.

525
00:30:51.416 --> 00:30:52.416
They're coming.

526
00:30:53.458 --> 00:30:56.583
- We need to have faith.
- Faith? What faith?

527
00:30:57.083 --> 00:30:59.875
Don't talk this way
in front of the younger guys.

528
00:30:59.958 --> 00:31:01.916
If you tell them,
you'll destroy their morale.

529
00:31:02.750 --> 00:31:06.083
You guys are the oldest ones here,
and you have a responsibility.

530
00:31:07.208 --> 00:31:08.541
[sighs]

531
00:31:09.500 --> 00:31:10.916
They <i>will</i> rescue us.

532
00:31:16.833 --> 00:31:19.541
- We won't last like this.
- How long can we survive?

533
00:31:20.250 --> 00:31:22.208
- [Roberto] Know the rule of three?
- [Fito] No.

534
00:31:22.291 --> 00:31:24.000
[Roberto] Three minutes without air,

535
00:31:24.083 --> 00:31:26.958
three days without water,
and three weeks without food.

536
00:31:27.041 --> 00:31:28.791
Three weeks without food?

537
00:31:28.875 --> 00:31:30.666
I haven't eaten in three days.
I'm starving.

538
00:31:30.750 --> 00:31:33.625
It's a lot worse here.
There's the altitude and the cold.

539
00:31:33.708 --> 00:31:36.458
We're burning three
or four times as many calories.

540
00:31:36.541 --> 00:31:38.541
Roque told us about the batteries.

541
00:31:39.500 --> 00:31:40.900
They were in the tail of the plane.

542
00:31:41.833 --> 00:31:45.583
In my opinion, we should go up there,
where the plane crashed,

543
00:31:46.083 --> 00:31:47.750
and get the radio working.

544
00:31:49.375 --> 00:31:50.291
[Fito grunts]

545
00:31:50.375 --> 00:31:52.208
[tense, rhythmic music playing]

546
00:32:38.541 --> 00:32:40.541
[panting]

547
00:32:43.500 --> 00:32:45.500
[tense music building]

548
00:32:48.458 --> 00:32:50.458
[foreboding choir music rises]

549
00:32:54.166 --> 00:32:55.916
[music subsides]

550
00:32:56.000 --> 00:32:57.083
[Numa whistles]

551
00:32:58.000 --> 00:32:59.125
We gotta keep going!

552
00:32:59.208 --> 00:33:00.250
The snow is still firm!

553
00:33:00.333 --> 00:33:03.416
- Let's take advantage of that!
- Numa! Save your energy!

554
00:33:03.500 --> 00:33:06.125
- [exhales]
- [Roberto] I don't want to carry you back.

555
00:33:09.500 --> 00:33:10.625
[Carlitos] Fito.

556
00:33:12.125 --> 00:33:13.125
What happened?

557
00:33:14.416 --> 00:33:16.166
You can't see the plane.

558
00:33:16.250 --> 00:33:18.416
[sighs, breathing shakily]

559
00:33:27.000 --> 00:33:29.250
They won't find it,
even if they fly over us.

560
00:33:31.416 --> 00:33:34.125
[thunderous crackling]

561
00:33:40.791 --> 00:33:43.666
[rumbling echoes across valley]

562
00:33:44.833 --> 00:33:45.833
We're going back!

563
00:33:45.875 --> 00:33:48.958
[panting]

564
00:33:49.041 --> 00:33:50.416
[silence falls]

565
00:33:52.125 --> 00:33:54.208
[Numa] <i>It's been six days without food.</i>

566
00:33:54.291 --> 00:33:56.291
[wind gusting]

567
00:33:58.666 --> 00:34:01.166
[Numa] <i>Last night,
we split what we had left.</i>

568
00:34:02.250 --> 00:34:03.708
<i>A pack of crackers.</i>

569
00:34:04.458 --> 00:34:05.750
<i>There's nothing else.</i>

570
00:34:11.708 --> 00:34:13.708
[panting]

571
00:34:25.583 --> 00:34:27.083
[breathing heavily]

572
00:34:35.625 --> 00:34:38.083
[spits]

573
00:34:38.166 --> 00:34:40.166
[all shivering]

574
00:35:03.333 --> 00:35:04.250
[smacks lips]

575
00:35:04.333 --> 00:35:05.750
[exhales, gulps]

576
00:35:07.000 --> 00:35:08.083
[crunches]

577
00:35:09.125 --> 00:35:10.208
[sighs]

578
00:35:21.166 --> 00:35:23.166
[wind gusting]

579
00:35:24.416 --> 00:35:26.583
[quietly] Carlitos came over
to tell me something.

580
00:35:28.625 --> 00:35:30.958
He says that Nando's losing his mind.

581
00:35:31.625 --> 00:35:34.958
<i>Last night, he went up to him
and said he wasn't gonna starve to death.</i>

582
00:35:35.041 --> 00:35:36.541
I'm not gonna starve to death.

583
00:35:36.625 --> 00:35:38.541
[Fito] <i>That he'd eat the bodies
if he had to.</i>

584
00:35:38.625 --> 00:35:40.833
If I have to, I'll eat the bodies.

585
00:35:48.000 --> 00:35:50.208
I told him
that we don't have another option.

586
00:36:01.375 --> 00:36:03.958
If we wanna get rescued,
we gotta stay alive.

587
00:36:07.083 --> 00:36:09.208
And to stay alive, we need to eat.

588
00:36:14.583 --> 00:36:17.250
[wind rattling against fuselage]

589
00:36:19.291 --> 00:36:21.291
[all shivering]

590
00:36:36.708 --> 00:36:37.708
Marcelo.

591
00:36:40.458 --> 00:36:42.041
We're dying.

592
00:36:44.250 --> 00:36:46.208
We're starving, and they're not coming.

593
00:36:47.083 --> 00:36:50.791
- We're wasting ourselves away.
- Seven days and nights without food.

594
00:36:51.291 --> 00:36:53.875
Nothing. If we don't eat, we're gonna die.

595
00:36:54.541 --> 00:36:55.625
Eat what?

596
00:36:58.708 --> 00:37:00.458
Are you crazy, Roberto?

597
00:37:00.541 --> 00:37:02.666
You gonna make everyone else crazy too?

598
00:37:02.750 --> 00:37:03.916
There's food outside.

599
00:37:10.916 --> 00:37:13.166
[Roberto] There's protein outside.
Energy that we need.

600
00:37:13.250 --> 00:37:15.041
Do you know what's crazy?
To go on like this!

601
00:37:15.125 --> 00:37:16.125
Roberto!

602
00:37:19.583 --> 00:37:22.500
Roberto's right. We're talking
about living or dying, Marcelo.

603
00:37:22.583 --> 00:37:25.208
And if help arrives
in two days, then what, Fito?

604
00:37:25.291 --> 00:37:26.875
Can't we wait a couple more days?

605
00:37:26.958 --> 00:37:29.375
- Know what happens when you stop eating?
- Roberto!

606
00:37:32.583 --> 00:37:34.208
The body dries out. Just like plants.

607
00:37:34.291 --> 00:37:36.916
You can't use your brain.
Because it dries out too, Marcelo.

608
00:37:37.000 --> 00:37:39.583
- My pee is black.
- Yeah, my pee is black too.

609
00:37:39.666 --> 00:37:40.958
If we do it...

610
00:37:42.541 --> 00:37:44.750
what will happen to us?
Will God forgive us?

611
00:37:44.833 --> 00:37:47.500
God put us in this situation.
He'll understand we need to survive.

612
00:37:47.583 --> 00:37:49.583
God has nothing to do with this.

613
00:37:49.666 --> 00:37:51.125
I'm sorry, Marcelo.

614
00:37:51.208 --> 00:37:52.875
It's luck that brought us here.

615
00:37:52.958 --> 00:37:54.375
- Bad luck.
- [Arturo] It's meat.

616
00:37:54.458 --> 00:37:57.375
- It's people we love, Arturo.
- And how do you cut up a body?

617
00:37:58.125 --> 00:37:59.666
And who would even do it?

618
00:38:02.750 --> 00:38:05.083
[Fito sighs] Me.

619
00:38:07.291 --> 00:38:08.458
[quietly] I'll do it.

620
00:38:08.958 --> 00:38:11.583
- I will too.
- [woman] I'm not eating them.

621
00:38:12.625 --> 00:38:14.250
That's something I refuse to do.

622
00:38:15.541 --> 00:38:17.666
Is it legal to eat a dead person?

623
00:38:18.166 --> 00:38:19.916
Won't we go to prison if we do it?

624
00:38:20.416 --> 00:38:23.291
- It would be like organ donation.
- What's wrong with you?

625
00:38:23.375 --> 00:38:27.333
For it to be organ donation,
you need to have the donor's consent.

626
00:38:27.416 --> 00:38:29.375
It's a crime, Marcelo.

627
00:38:29.458 --> 00:38:33.208
We can't just take, defile, and desecrate
someone's body without consent.

628
00:38:33.291 --> 00:38:35.791
- We need to eat, Numa.
- We don't have the right to.

629
00:38:35.875 --> 00:38:38.791
And don't I have the right
to do everything I can to survive?

630
00:38:42.125 --> 00:38:43.875
Who's gonna take that from me? You?

631
00:38:54.666 --> 00:38:56.458
- [crying]
- [Marcelo sniffles]

632
00:38:56.541 --> 00:38:58.541
[Pancho sobbing]

633
00:39:04.916 --> 00:39:06.291
[sobs, sniffles]

634
00:39:06.375 --> 00:39:08.375
[frozen wind howling]

635
00:39:21.875 --> 00:39:23.875
[Numa breathing shakily]

636
00:39:29.958 --> 00:39:33.666
[haunting instrumental music playing]

637
00:40:26.333 --> 00:40:30.291
- [fuselage creaking]
- [wind howling outside]

638
00:40:45.625 --> 00:40:47.625
[labored breathing]

639
00:40:50.125 --> 00:40:51.916
[Susy exhales heavily]

640
00:40:58.333 --> 00:40:59.375
Susy?

641
00:41:00.666 --> 00:41:02.583
Susy. Susy, breathe.

642
00:41:03.166 --> 00:41:04.833
No, no, no. Susana.

643
00:41:05.333 --> 00:41:08.250
Susana, come on. No. No. Gustavo!

644
00:41:08.875 --> 00:41:10.333
Gustavo, help me, please.

645
00:41:10.875 --> 00:41:13.583
- Susana. Please help me!
- [Gustavo] What's wrong?

646
00:41:13.666 --> 00:41:15.346
[Nando] She's not breathing. I don't know.

647
00:41:15.375 --> 00:41:17.875
[Gustavo] Okay. Put her legs over there.
I'll hold her head.

648
00:41:17.958 --> 00:41:20.583
[Nando] Roberto.
She's not breathing, Roberto.

649
00:41:20.666 --> 00:41:22.706
- Help her.
- [Roberto] Bring her here. Right there.

650
00:41:23.291 --> 00:41:25.541
Help me, Gustavo! Hurry!

651
00:41:25.625 --> 00:41:27.958
- [Gustavo] She's not breathing.
- [Roberto] Susy!

652
00:41:28.708 --> 00:41:30.958
[Numa] <i>Coco Nicolich
wrote a letter to his parents.</i>

653
00:41:31.041 --> 00:41:33.041
[somber piano music playing]

654
00:41:35.166 --> 00:41:36.583
[Numa] <i>"Dear Mom and Dad,</i>

655
00:41:37.708 --> 00:41:40.916
<i>I'm writing to you
eight days after the plane crashed."</i>

656
00:41:45.208 --> 00:41:46.833
<i>"We're in a beautiful place,</i>

657
00:41:47.833 --> 00:41:51.333
<i>completely surrounded by mountains,
with a lake nearby,</i>

658
00:41:51.416 --> 00:41:53.958
<i>that will unfreeze when the thaw starts."</i>

659
00:41:56.041 --> 00:41:57.250
<i>"We're all doing fine."</i>

660
00:41:58.541 --> 00:42:01.208
<i>"As of now, there are 27 survivors."</i>

661
00:42:03.083 --> 00:42:06.083
<i>"Nando Parrado's sister
passed away today."</i>

662
00:42:08.666 --> 00:42:10.208
<i>"I miss you very much."</i>

663
00:42:10.291 --> 00:42:13.166
[wind gusting]

664
00:42:13.250 --> 00:42:15.458
[Numa] <i>"And I'm constantly praying to God,</i>

665
00:42:17.125 --> 00:42:20.708
<i>that he at least
lets me see you one last time."</i>

666
00:42:33.958 --> 00:42:35.958
[wind picks up]

667
00:42:41.291 --> 00:42:42.791
This is a cemetery.

668
00:42:46.791 --> 00:42:47.875
[exhales resolutely]

669
00:42:48.958 --> 00:42:50.541
And I'm not staying here.

670
00:42:53.958 --> 00:42:55.958
[thunder rumbling in distance]

671
00:42:58.625 --> 00:42:59.958
[thunder crashes]

672
00:43:00.041 --> 00:43:02.000
[man] It hurts! My stomach hurts!

673
00:43:02.083 --> 00:43:04.250
[woman] I know, Moncho.
You need to calm down.

674
00:43:04.333 --> 00:43:06.291
- Just breathe.
- I can't breathe. [sobs]

675
00:43:06.375 --> 00:43:09.291
Look at me, Moncho. Look at me. Breathe.

676
00:43:09.375 --> 00:43:10.791
- I don't want to!
- Just breathe.

677
00:43:10.875 --> 00:43:13.500
- [Moncho] I can't! I can't! Help me!
- [woman] Yes, you can.

678
00:43:13.583 --> 00:43:14.583
Look at me and breathe!

679
00:43:14.666 --> 00:43:17.000
[Moncho] I gotta get outta here!
I'm suffocating!

680
00:43:17.083 --> 00:43:20.125
[woman] You can't go outside now, Moncho.
Look at me. You have to calm down.

681
00:43:20.208 --> 00:43:22.892
- [Moncho] I don't want to die here.
- [woman] You're not going to die.

682
00:43:22.916 --> 00:43:25.756
- [Moncho] I don't want to die here!
- [woman] You're not dying, Moncho.

683
00:43:26.416 --> 00:43:30.541
{\an8}DAY 9
OCTOBER 21, 1972

684
00:43:31.375 --> 00:43:33.375
[all shivering]

685
00:43:41.958 --> 00:43:44.833
If I die,
I give you permission to feed on my body.

686
00:43:49.500 --> 00:43:51.000
So you can keep on living.

687
00:43:55.541 --> 00:43:57.750
I give you my consent as well.

688
00:43:58.333 --> 00:43:59.333
And you have mine.

689
00:44:00.333 --> 00:44:01.708
You also have my permission.

690
00:44:24.125 --> 00:44:26.083
[tense music playing]

691
00:44:26.166 --> 00:44:29.375
[Moncho] Our Father, who art in heaven,
hallowed be thy name.

692
00:44:29.458 --> 00:44:33.916
Thy kingdom come, thy will be done
on earth as it is in heaven.

693
00:44:34.000 --> 00:44:35.416
Give us this day our daily bread.

694
00:44:35.500 --> 00:44:36.666
And forgive us our trespasses

695
00:44:36.750 --> 00:44:38.833
as we forgive those
who trespass against us.

696
00:44:38.916 --> 00:44:41.666
And lead us not into temptation,
but deliver us from evil. Amen.

697
00:44:41.750 --> 00:44:44.000
Our Father, who art in heaven,
hallowed be thy name.

698
00:44:44.083 --> 00:44:44.958
Thy kingdom come.

699
00:44:45.041 --> 00:44:47.000
Thy will be done
on earth as it is in heaven.

700
00:44:47.083 --> 00:44:49.000
Give us this day our daily bread.

701
00:44:49.083 --> 00:44:50.541
And forgive us our trespasses

702
00:44:50.625 --> 00:44:52.750
as we forgive those
who trespass against us.

703
00:44:52.833 --> 00:44:56.166
And lead us not into temptation,
but deliver us from evil. Amen.

704
00:44:56.250 --> 00:44:57.958
On earth as it is in heaven.

705
00:44:58.041 --> 00:45:00.561
Give us this day our daily bread.
And forgive us our trespasses.

706
00:45:00.625 --> 00:45:02.875
- [gasps]
- [Moncho] And lead us not into temptation.

707
00:45:02.958 --> 00:45:04.791
But deliver us from evil. Amen.

708
00:45:04.875 --> 00:45:06.416
[crying softly]

709
00:45:14.916 --> 00:45:16.041
[Nando grunts]

710
00:45:24.125 --> 00:45:26.000
I'm sorry. [sniffles]

711
00:45:34.125 --> 00:45:35.541
[Roque] Sorry, Marcelo.

712
00:45:37.916 --> 00:45:39.125
[Marcelo sniffles]

713
00:45:39.208 --> 00:45:40.666
[man 1] Sorry, Marcelo.

714
00:45:44.750 --> 00:45:46.166
[man 2] Will God forgive us?

715
00:45:48.083 --> 00:45:50.666
[man 3] We don't have a choice.
I'm sorry, Marcelo.

716
00:45:54.208 --> 00:45:56.041
[Marcelo breathing shakily]

717
00:46:00.041 --> 00:46:02.041
[panting]

718
00:46:19.500 --> 00:46:20.708
[sighs]

719
00:46:30.166 --> 00:46:32.166
[somber instrumental music playing]

720
00:46:47.166 --> 00:46:49.500
[shivering] Don't give me
that look, Coche.

721
00:46:52.875 --> 00:46:54.791
I'm not giving you a look.

722
00:46:57.000 --> 00:46:58.250
[shudders]

723
00:47:08.166 --> 00:47:09.333
[group grunting]

724
00:47:15.791 --> 00:47:18.875
[Numa] <i>The Strauch cousins
have the most difficult job.</i>

725
00:47:21.250 --> 00:47:22.958
<i>The one no one wants to do.</i>

726
00:47:24.625 --> 00:47:26.458
<i>Fito chooses the bodies.</i>

727
00:47:28.000 --> 00:47:29.916
<i>And they cut them up in secret.</i>

728
00:47:32.458 --> 00:47:34.375
<i>Away from everyone else.</i>

729
00:47:36.625 --> 00:47:39.291
<i>That's how they keep
the ones who eat sane.</i>

730
00:47:46.833 --> 00:47:48.833
[somber music swells]

731
00:47:57.750 --> 00:47:58.750
Hey!

732
00:47:58.791 --> 00:48:00.750
- [Coco] What?
- [Coche] I found something!

733
00:48:05.125 --> 00:48:06.250
[Roy] A radio!

734
00:48:09.416 --> 00:48:10.708
It's all wet.

735
00:48:11.208 --> 00:48:12.666
Come on, Roy. Fix it.

736
00:48:22.125 --> 00:48:24.583
[Numa] <i>Those of us who don't eat
keep watching the sky.</i>

737
00:48:28.750 --> 00:48:30.250
<i>Waiting for a sign.</i>

738
00:48:31.333 --> 00:48:34.708
- [static crackles]
- [indistinct radio chatter]

739
00:48:40.666 --> 00:48:42.000
[Coco] Left or right?

740
00:48:43.583 --> 00:48:44.458
Higher, Coco.

741
00:48:44.541 --> 00:48:46.501
If you want it higher,
we'll need to get more wire

742
00:48:46.541 --> 00:48:48.958
and tie it to a pole or something.

743
00:48:50.041 --> 00:48:53.250
[Roy] Hold it there.
A little bit to the left.

744
00:48:54.625 --> 00:48:55.875
A bit more.

745
00:48:57.958 --> 00:49:00.083
Less. A little to the right.

746
00:49:00.166 --> 00:49:01.166
There.

747
00:49:04.375 --> 00:49:06.375
[indistinct chatter continues outside]

748
00:49:14.000 --> 00:49:15.125
[Pancho sniffles]

749
00:49:22.791 --> 00:49:23.791
Take this.

750
00:49:27.291 --> 00:49:28.416
What is that?

751
00:49:30.125 --> 00:49:32.541
Eat it. It's easier with snow.

752
00:49:32.625 --> 00:49:33.916
[Numa] No, thank you.

753
00:49:34.000 --> 00:49:36.416
- I'll be okay.
- [Pancho sniffles, sighs]

754
00:49:38.583 --> 00:49:40.208
You have to eat, Numa.

755
00:49:44.625 --> 00:49:46.333
It's not right, Pancho.

756
00:49:48.000 --> 00:49:49.000
[sighs]

757
00:49:50.333 --> 00:49:54.250
- [man 1 cries out] No!
- [Numa gasps]

758
00:49:56.125 --> 00:49:59.125
[screaming and sobbing outside]

759
00:49:59.875 --> 00:50:02.375
Why?! [screams]

760
00:50:02.458 --> 00:50:06.666
[reporter on radio] <i>This is</i> Spectator.
<i>We're coming to you with new information.</i>

761
00:50:06.750 --> 00:50:09.750
<i>The search for the Uruguayan plane
that crashed in the Andean Mountain Range</i>

762
00:50:09.833 --> 00:50:12.916
<i>with the rugby team Old Christians,
has come to an end.</i>

763
00:50:14.041 --> 00:50:16.083
<i>In the ten days required by the protocol,</i>

764
00:50:16.166 --> 00:50:19.375
<i>66 search and rescue missions
were conducted,</i>

765
00:50:19.458 --> 00:50:22.500
<i>using 17 planes from the Chilean Air Force</i>

766
00:50:22.583 --> 00:50:26.083
<i>as well as aircrafts of the Uruguayan
and Argentinian Air Forces,</i>

767
00:50:26.166 --> 00:50:27.916
<i>but to no avail.</i>

768
00:50:28.000 --> 00:50:30.708
<i>Search efforts will resume
early next year,</i>

769
00:50:31.791 --> 00:50:33.391
<i>when the thawing of the ice will provide</i>

770
00:50:33.416 --> 00:50:36.500
<i>better conditions of visibility
to find the wreckage.</i>

771
00:50:36.583 --> 00:50:38.875
<i>The Chilean Air Force's rescue service</i>

772
00:50:38.958 --> 00:50:42.916
<i>has reported that, in the 34 air accidents
that have occurred in the Andes,</i>

773
00:50:43.000 --> 00:50:45.166
<i>no survivors have ever been found.</i>

774
00:50:45.958 --> 00:50:48.666
<i>We'll return with more news
after a commercial break.</i>

775
00:50:48.750 --> 00:50:50.750
[cheerful radio jingle playing]

776
00:50:52.166 --> 00:50:55.666
[announcer 1, in Spanish]
<i>Made with premium quality parts.</i>

777
00:50:55.750 --> 00:50:57.791
<i>Beautiful colors and designs.</i>

778
00:50:58.625 --> 00:51:01.708
[announcer 2] <i>Customizable,
with three different models.</i>

779
00:51:01.791 --> 00:51:06.166
<i>Bicicletas Victoria,
the leading bicycle brand.</i>

780
00:51:06.250 --> 00:51:08.000
[jingle fades]

781
00:51:08.083 --> 00:51:09.333
[in English] I was wrong.

782
00:51:11.708 --> 00:51:14.208
I begged you to wait
to be rescued for nothing.

783
00:51:18.041 --> 00:51:20.000
But if I can ask you for one more thing,

784
00:51:22.458 --> 00:51:24.000
I'm asking you to eat.

785
00:51:24.083 --> 00:51:26.083
[tense music playing]

786
00:51:31.708 --> 00:51:33.125
[coughs]

787
00:51:33.208 --> 00:51:34.958
[breathing shakily]

788
00:51:39.166 --> 00:51:41.333
[Marcelo] <i>The only thing we have left
is our life.</i>

789
00:51:41.416 --> 00:51:43.500
<i>And we have to fight for it.</i>

790
00:51:44.333 --> 00:51:45.500
[Numa sighs]

791
00:51:45.583 --> 00:51:47.583
[ominous orchestral music playing]

792
00:51:54.791 --> 00:51:57.250
[Numa] <i>We went up to look
for the tail of the plane.</i>

793
00:51:57.333 --> 00:51:58.708
<i>Without telling anyone.</i>

794
00:51:58.791 --> 00:52:00.000
<i>With no plan.</i>

795
00:52:01.375 --> 00:52:03.875
<i>We need to find batteries for the radio.</i>

796
00:52:07.916 --> 00:52:09.916
[group panting]

797
00:52:24.000 --> 00:52:25.000
[Numa] Over there.

798
00:52:38.708 --> 00:52:39.750
[sniffles]

799
00:52:49.208 --> 00:52:50.750
[sighs deeply]

800
00:52:53.958 --> 00:52:55.333
I'm here, Gastón.

801
00:52:55.875 --> 00:52:57.875
[speaking inaudibly]

802
00:53:26.250 --> 00:53:27.500
[grunts]

803
00:53:29.083 --> 00:53:31.250
That's Daniel Shaw, Fito's cousin.

804
00:53:31.916 --> 00:53:34.250
He was behind me on the plane
and flew out.

805
00:53:34.875 --> 00:53:36.291
[Maspons] Sun's going down.

806
00:53:36.375 --> 00:53:37.833
- We should go back.
- No.

807
00:53:39.083 --> 00:53:40.708
Let's look some more. Please.

808
00:53:41.791 --> 00:53:45.208
If we found all these things here,
the tail shouldn't be far behind.

809
00:53:47.416 --> 00:53:48.958
[grunting]

810
00:53:52.041 --> 00:53:53.041
[groans]

811
00:53:55.291 --> 00:53:57.291
[panting]

812
00:54:01.166 --> 00:54:02.375
Who's up there?

813
00:54:03.291 --> 00:54:06.333
Numa, Gustavo, and Maspons.

814
00:54:07.958 --> 00:54:09.500
They left with nothing.

815
00:54:10.458 --> 00:54:12.958
The temperature up there
must drop 80 or 90 degrees.

816
00:54:13.875 --> 00:54:15.541
<i>And it's gonna be night soon.</i>

817
00:54:16.708 --> 00:54:18.708
[cold air rushes]

818
00:54:24.333 --> 00:54:27.333
[Numa] <i>The sun had melted the snow,
and we were knee-deep in it.</i>

819
00:54:27.958 --> 00:54:30.083
[Numa] No, that way!

820
00:54:30.166 --> 00:54:32.166
[panting]

821
00:54:38.333 --> 00:54:42.333
[Numa] <i>We can barely keep going,
and the night traps us.</i>

822
00:54:42.416 --> 00:54:44.416
[raging wind]

823
00:54:45.875 --> 00:54:47.583
Everyone, get closer! Get closer.

824
00:54:49.041 --> 00:54:51.375
[moaning]

825
00:54:51.958 --> 00:54:53.208
Calm down!

826
00:54:53.291 --> 00:54:54.750
Come on!

827
00:54:54.833 --> 00:54:56.750
Please, Lord,
don't let us freeze to death.

828
00:54:56.833 --> 00:54:59.166
[Gustavo] Shake the ice off my back!

829
00:55:00.625 --> 00:55:02.625
[all groaning]

830
00:55:02.708 --> 00:55:05.458
[freezing wind picks up]

831
00:55:05.541 --> 00:55:07.541
[silence falls]

832
00:55:11.333 --> 00:55:14.375
[wind gusting]

833
00:55:29.208 --> 00:55:31.208
[gasping]

834
00:55:39.333 --> 00:55:40.958
[groans weakly]

835
00:55:46.541 --> 00:55:48.541
[shivering]

836
00:55:54.500 --> 00:55:56.500
[breathing shakily]

837
00:55:59.458 --> 00:56:01.708
[Numa] <i>The more we try to get out,</i>

838
00:56:02.750 --> 00:56:04.666
<i>the more the mountain resists.</i>

839
00:56:13.791 --> 00:56:16.416
[man 1 screams]

840
00:56:18.708 --> 00:56:19.875
[man 2] Hey!

841
00:56:27.125 --> 00:56:29.208
[softly] Gus, eat.

842
00:56:32.416 --> 00:56:33.541
[Nando] So, Numa.

843
00:56:35.750 --> 00:56:37.000
What did you see up there?

844
00:56:42.791 --> 00:56:43.958
Numa.

845
00:56:44.041 --> 00:56:45.041
Tell me.

846
00:56:46.041 --> 00:56:47.791
Only snow and mountains.

847
00:56:48.458 --> 00:56:49.875
[Nando] In every direction?

848
00:56:50.500 --> 00:56:53.958
[Numa] As far as I could see,
that's all there is.

849
00:56:54.041 --> 00:56:55.041
And to the west?

850
00:56:55.750 --> 00:56:58.500
- See anything behind that ice wall?
- [Numa] No.

851
00:57:00.791 --> 00:57:02.416
You can't see anything.

852
00:57:03.833 --> 00:57:05.083
Chile's right behind it.

853
00:57:07.375 --> 00:57:08.750
We need to go there.

854
00:57:11.166 --> 00:57:14.416
But you gotta eat, Numa.
Or you won't make it to Chile.

855
00:57:20.625 --> 00:57:21.708
[Numa sighs]

856
00:57:31.500 --> 00:57:33.833
[somber instrumental music playing]

857
00:57:38.416 --> 00:57:40.416
[breathing shakily]

858
00:57:52.875 --> 00:57:53.875
[quietly] Come on.

859
00:57:53.958 --> 00:57:55.125
[Numa sighs heavily]

860
00:58:01.958 --> 00:58:04.375
[crying softly]

861
00:58:18.125 --> 00:58:20.791
[Numa] <i>I don't chew
more than two or three times.</i>

862
00:58:22.875 --> 00:58:24.875
<i>And I force myself to swallow.</i>

863
00:58:35.083 --> 00:58:38.250
<i>For the first time,
I imagine the possibility</i>

864
00:58:38.333 --> 00:58:41.916
<i>that feels increasingly real
of not getting back home.</i>

865
00:58:45.333 --> 00:58:47.041
<i>But I look at Nando, and I feel hope.</i>

866
00:58:47.125 --> 00:58:49.125
[wind whipping]

867
00:58:50.416 --> 00:58:53.166
[Numa] <i>He trains every day,
obsessed with one idea.</i>

868
00:58:54.291 --> 00:58:58.625
<i>Beyond that mountain
lie the green valleys of Chile.</i>

869
00:59:00.458 --> 00:59:02.125
<i>Climbing it is suicide.</i>

870
00:59:04.250 --> 00:59:06.708
[frigid air rushing]

871
00:59:08.833 --> 00:59:10.166
[Numa] <i>But I'm going with him.</i>

872
00:59:12.000 --> 00:59:16.083
{\an8}DAY 17
FIFTH DAY OF THE STORM

873
00:59:16.625 --> 00:59:18.583
[group laughing and chatting]

874
00:59:18.666 --> 00:59:20.208
[man 1] Getting worse.

875
00:59:22.000 --> 00:59:23.750
Okay, Vasco. Check this out.

876
00:59:24.750 --> 00:59:26.625
- <i>'Cause your rhyme was all talk</i>
- [chuckles]

877
00:59:28.500 --> 00:59:30.958
<i>Tell me, why don't you get up
And go out for a quick walk?</i>

878
00:59:31.041 --> 00:59:32.583
[all laugh]

879
00:59:32.666 --> 00:59:34.250
[man 1] You're an idiot, Bobby!

880
00:59:34.333 --> 00:59:36.875
- [man 2] Okay, Carlitos.
- Yeah, Carlitos.

881
00:59:36.958 --> 00:59:40.583
<i>We can barely fit 27 of us
But that's all right</i>

882
00:59:40.666 --> 00:59:43.958
<i>While we're all cramped in here
Up in the presidential suite, they're fine</i>

883
00:59:44.041 --> 00:59:46.458
[all laugh]

884
00:59:46.541 --> 00:59:48.875
[Arturo] <i>While a terrible tragedy unfolds</i>

885
00:59:48.958 --> 00:59:52.666
<i>I want to escape
Yet I see many heroes without capes</i>

886
00:59:52.750 --> 00:59:54.166
- [all chuckle]
- Aww.

887
00:59:54.250 --> 00:59:56.541
<i>And although sometimes
Anger overtakes me</i>

888
00:59:56.625 --> 00:59:59.500
<i>Standing by your side
Truly strengthens me</i>

889
00:59:59.583 --> 01:00:00.958
- [man 3] Deep!
- Oh!

890
01:00:01.041 --> 01:00:03.666
<i>Even though we're now freezing to death
On this plane</i>

891
01:00:04.541 --> 01:00:06.708
<i>I have Coco's warm feet here
And can't complain</i>

892
01:00:06.791 --> 01:00:08.041
[both laugh]

893
01:00:08.125 --> 01:00:10.666
<i>But, Coco
Don't get used to this situation</i>

894
01:00:10.750 --> 01:00:13.041
<i>We gotta get back to Uruguay
Our beloved nation</i>

895
01:00:13.125 --> 01:00:15.666
- [man 3] That's right!
- [Daniel] Come on, Coco. Go.

896
01:00:15.750 --> 01:00:17.583
Okay, but mine's kinda sentimental.

897
01:00:18.708 --> 01:00:21.500
<i>On October thirteenth
My mother's birthday I did miss</i>

898
01:00:22.250 --> 01:00:23.583
<i>So I humbly ask God</i>

899
01:00:24.458 --> 01:00:26.083
<i>To finally come home</i>

900
01:00:26.583 --> 01:00:28.541
<i>So I can give her a big kiss</i>

901
01:00:28.625 --> 01:00:30.065
- [man 4] Very sweet.
- [man 5] Nice.

902
01:00:31.666 --> 01:00:33.666
[Fito] <i>There are some decent people
In this space</i>

903
01:00:34.375 --> 01:00:37.041
<i>Yet some know not the candidates
For the presidential race</i>

904
01:00:37.541 --> 01:00:39.666
<i>They are a tremendous disgrace</i>

905
01:00:40.250 --> 01:00:41.458
[all chuckle]

906
01:00:41.541 --> 01:00:43.916
- [man 4] That was awful!
- [man 6] That's terrible!

907
01:00:44.000 --> 01:00:46.000
- All right.
- [man 4] Terrible. The worst.

908
01:00:46.083 --> 01:00:47.375
At least I tried, you know?

909
01:00:47.458 --> 01:00:49.250
- You guys didn't do anything.
- [all laugh]

910
01:00:49.333 --> 01:00:51.916
<i>Here in the mountains
The situation's intense</i>

911
01:00:52.916 --> 01:00:55.708
<i>It makes me wanna start running
Like a puma</i>

912
01:00:56.208 --> 01:00:58.208
<i>But I will not leave this place</i>

913
01:00:58.291 --> 01:01:00.791
<i>Without first hearing a rhyme
From the reserved Numa</i>

914
01:01:04.833 --> 01:01:06.541
[Numa] Uh... [chuckles]

915
01:01:06.625 --> 01:01:09.333
<i>On, uh, this extremely freezing mountain</i>

916
01:01:10.083 --> 01:01:12.666
<i>Where... not even a spider can walk</i>

917
01:01:13.541 --> 01:01:15.166
[all chuckle]

918
01:01:15.250 --> 01:01:18.291
<i>In the... in the fridge</i>

919
01:01:19.291 --> 01:01:22.166
<i>On the mountain of the frozen fridge</i>

920
01:01:22.250 --> 01:01:23.458
- Forget it.
- [all laugh]

921
01:01:24.958 --> 01:01:26.625
<i>Of the mountain...</i> All right.

922
01:01:26.708 --> 01:01:27.875
- [all cheer]
- Bravo! Good!

923
01:01:27.958 --> 01:01:28.958
Come on, Numa!

924
01:01:30.375 --> 01:01:31.875
- [man 6 whistles]
- Bravo!

925
01:01:32.541 --> 01:01:35.750
- [cheering continues]
- Hey, I tried.

926
01:01:35.833 --> 01:01:38.041
[loud knocking]

927
01:01:39.875 --> 01:01:41.875
[low rumbling]

928
01:01:43.958 --> 01:01:45.958
[fuselage rattling]

929
01:01:50.416 --> 01:01:51.958
[all scream]

930
01:01:54.541 --> 01:01:56.541
[silence falls]

931
01:01:57.833 --> 01:01:59.833
[snow crunching]

932
01:02:02.000 --> 01:02:04.041
[muffled screams]

933
01:02:09.541 --> 01:02:11.208
[gasping for air]

934
01:02:16.166 --> 01:02:18.708
[muffled screams continue under snow]

935
01:02:24.916 --> 01:02:27.666
[survivors screaming indistinctly]

936
01:02:27.750 --> 01:02:29.750
[wind howling]

937
01:02:31.625 --> 01:02:33.458
[panting]

938
01:02:34.416 --> 01:02:35.416
Roy!

939
01:02:35.500 --> 01:02:37.500
[icy wind rushing]

940
01:02:51.041 --> 01:02:53.041
[shivering]

941
01:02:54.000 --> 01:02:55.000
[man 2] Roy!

942
01:02:56.666 --> 01:03:00.375
- [man 1] Down there! Down there!
- Here! I'm here!

943
01:03:00.458 --> 01:03:03.250
[man 1] Dig! [grunting]

944
01:03:03.333 --> 01:03:04.625
[gasps]

945
01:03:06.166 --> 01:03:07.416
Fito!

946
01:03:07.500 --> 01:03:09.000
[screams]

947
01:03:09.083 --> 01:03:10.625
- [man 2] Tintín!
- Hey!

948
01:03:10.708 --> 01:03:12.708
- [Fito] Hold on!
- [man 3] Hold on!

949
01:03:12.791 --> 01:03:15.833
[Fito] Hold on! Hold on!
Hold on! We're getting you out!

950
01:03:15.916 --> 01:03:18.291
[screams]

951
01:03:18.375 --> 01:03:20.166
- [Roy] Coche, help.
- [Coche] Get him out!

952
01:03:20.250 --> 01:03:22.625
- [Fito] Dig! Come on!
- [man 5] Hold on!

953
01:03:22.708 --> 01:03:23.958
Hold on!

954
01:03:24.041 --> 01:03:25.208
[gasps]

955
01:03:25.291 --> 01:03:26.625
[man 6] Everyone, dig! Dig!

956
01:03:26.708 --> 01:03:28.791
[gasping for air]

957
01:03:28.875 --> 01:03:30.291
[muffled shouts]

958
01:03:30.375 --> 01:03:33.250
[Fito] Help! Help! Help!

959
01:03:33.333 --> 01:03:35.375
Hang in there, Numa!

960
01:03:35.458 --> 01:03:39.916
- Numa, I'll get you out!
- [Numa shouts, strains]

961
01:03:40.000 --> 01:03:42.000
[sounds distort]

962
01:03:44.000 --> 01:03:46.000
[shouts] No! Coco!

963
01:03:46.083 --> 01:03:47.583
[straining]

964
01:03:47.666 --> 01:03:49.083
[panting]

965
01:03:49.166 --> 01:03:50.291
[screams]

966
01:03:51.666 --> 01:03:52.833
- Over here!
- Coco!

967
01:03:53.750 --> 01:03:56.250
[Javier] Liliana's down there!
Don't step on her!

968
01:03:56.333 --> 01:03:58.541
Watch out! Liliana's down there!
For God's sake!

969
01:03:58.625 --> 01:04:01.416
Please, don't step on her!
Liliana's there!

970
01:04:01.500 --> 01:04:05.041
Liliana, hold on! Don't step on her!
Liliana's down there! Please!

971
01:04:05.125 --> 01:04:07.791
Don't step on her! Baby, I'll get you out!

972
01:04:07.875 --> 01:04:08.875
She's here!

973
01:04:08.958 --> 01:04:10.791
Coco! No!

974
01:04:10.875 --> 01:04:13.791
- Coco! Coco! Coco! Coco!
- [Javier] Help me!

975
01:04:14.958 --> 01:04:17.500
- [Carlitos] Coco!
- [all grunting]

976
01:04:19.250 --> 01:04:21.083
Breathe! Breathe! Breathe!

977
01:04:21.166 --> 01:04:23.250
Breathe, baby. Breathe.

978
01:04:23.333 --> 01:04:26.750
[softly] Breathe! Oh God!
Breathe, baby. Please.

979
01:04:26.833 --> 01:04:29.250
Breathe. Oh, baby. Just breathe.

980
01:04:29.333 --> 01:04:31.375
- [Carlitos] He's not breathing!
- [Javier] Breathe.

981
01:04:31.458 --> 01:04:32.458
[Carlitos] Hold on!

982
01:04:32.500 --> 01:04:34.333
Please breathe. [kisses]

983
01:04:34.416 --> 01:04:37.791
- [sighs, crying] No, my love, don't go.
- [shouting continues]

984
01:04:37.875 --> 01:04:39.875
[fuselage rattling]

985
01:04:39.958 --> 01:04:41.416
[survivors scream]

986
01:04:43.291 --> 01:04:44.458
[man 6] What's that noise?

987
01:04:44.541 --> 01:04:46.875
[man 4] What's happening?
What's happening?

988
01:04:46.958 --> 01:04:47.958
[Numa] What is that?

989
01:04:48.041 --> 01:04:50.041
[low rumbling]

990
01:04:57.958 --> 01:05:00.583
[silence falls]

991
01:05:00.666 --> 01:05:01.958
[survivors grunting]

992
01:05:06.791 --> 01:05:08.791
[panting]

993
01:05:13.583 --> 01:05:14.750
[man 1] Come on.

994
01:05:16.875 --> 01:05:18.851
- [man 2] There's air.
- [man 3] Oxygen's coming in.

995
01:05:18.875 --> 01:05:20.333
- [man 2] There's air.
- Yes.

996
01:05:22.333 --> 01:05:23.666
Is everyone okay?

997
01:05:24.166 --> 01:05:26.625
- Arturo?
- I'm alive!

998
01:05:26.708 --> 01:05:28.750
Javier's alive. Liliana's gone.

999
01:05:28.833 --> 01:05:30.750
- [Fito] Vasco?
- Right here. I'm alive.

1000
01:05:30.833 --> 01:05:33.666
- I'm alive too! It's Roberto.
- Yeah, I'm alive! It's Moncho.

1001
01:05:33.750 --> 01:05:35.250
Pedro Algorta here.

1002
01:05:35.333 --> 01:05:37.375
[Fito] Diego? Diego?

1003
01:05:37.458 --> 01:05:39.083
Diego's dead, Fito!

1004
01:05:39.958 --> 01:05:41.666
He's gone. And Roque. Roque too.

1005
01:05:41.750 --> 01:05:42.875
Maspons couldn't make it.

1006
01:05:42.958 --> 01:05:45.958
- It's Nando. I'm alive.
- Enrique and Juan Carlos are dead.

1007
01:05:46.041 --> 01:05:47.521
- [Fito] Tintín, you okay?
- I'm here.

1008
01:05:47.583 --> 01:05:48.708
Coco?

1009
01:05:49.541 --> 01:05:52.458
- Coco?
- Coco's dead. This is Roy.

1010
01:05:52.541 --> 01:05:55.583
- And Marcelo? Marcelo?
- [man 4] Marcelo!

1011
01:05:55.666 --> 01:05:57.125
- [Fito] Marcelo!
- Marcelo!

1012
01:05:57.208 --> 01:05:59.208
- Marcelo? [sighs]
- [man 4] Captain!

1013
01:05:59.291 --> 01:06:00.541
[Fito, echoing] Marcelo!

1014
01:06:00.625 --> 01:06:02.625
[ethereal chimes playing]

1015
01:06:08.333 --> 01:06:09.541
[ice cracking]

1016
01:06:09.625 --> 01:06:12.083
[Numa] <i>Marcelo was buried.</i>

1017
01:06:14.458 --> 01:06:17.541
<i>He stopped feeling cold
because he didn't feel anything.</i>

1018
01:06:19.708 --> 01:06:21.875
<i>And to stop feeling here is a relief.</i>

1019
01:06:24.791 --> 01:06:28.125
<i>For 17 days,
we've waited for a moment like that.</i>

1020
01:06:30.458 --> 01:06:32.166
<i>A moment of calm.</i>

1021
01:06:35.125 --> 01:06:37.000
<i>A second of quiet.</i>

1022
01:06:38.916 --> 01:06:40.916
[music fades]

1023
01:06:41.000 --> 01:06:42.833
[wind howling above]

1024
01:06:42.916 --> 01:06:44.916
[fuselage creaking]

1025
01:06:56.583 --> 01:07:00.291
- How much snow could we have on top?
- It could be the entire mountain.

1026
01:07:02.041 --> 01:07:04.250
Everyone, pray! Right now!

1027
01:07:04.333 --> 01:07:06.750
[survivors] "And blessed is the fruit
of thy womb, Jesus."

1028
01:07:06.833 --> 01:07:10.125
- [group continues praying]
- [Numa] <i>Today is October 30th.</i>

1029
01:07:11.000 --> 01:07:12.625
<i>Today is my birthday.</i>

1030
01:07:14.416 --> 01:07:15.916
<i>I'm turning 25.</i>

1031
01:07:17.000 --> 01:07:18.875
[creaking fades]

1032
01:07:19.958 --> 01:07:22.250
[Numa] <i>Today it's hard
not to think of home.</i>

1033
01:07:24.875 --> 01:07:27.750
[somber instrumental music playing]

1034
01:07:37.875 --> 01:07:40.625
[wind whistling above]

1035
01:07:48.541 --> 01:07:51.291
If light comes in,
we shouldn't be too deep in the snow.

1036
01:08:21.458 --> 01:08:23.125
How long do you think we'll be here?

1037
01:08:24.000 --> 01:08:26.000
We can't go out until the storm's over.

1038
01:08:32.708 --> 01:08:34.708
[fuselage creaking]

1039
01:08:38.875 --> 01:08:41.708
[music dies out]

1040
01:08:44.500 --> 01:08:49.958
DAY 18
TWO DAYS BURIED

1041
01:08:55.833 --> 01:08:57.833
[Numa] <i>The hunger is unbearable.</i>

1042
01:09:01.833 --> 01:09:06.666
<i>Till now, the Strauch cousins
have been able to make the meat just meat.</i>

1043
01:09:07.958 --> 01:09:09.416
<i>Meat without a name.</i>

1044
01:09:10.500 --> 01:09:11.916
<i>Without a face.</i>

1045
01:09:14.541 --> 01:09:16.291
<i>But that's impossible here.</i>

1046
01:09:19.958 --> 01:09:23.958
[Roberto] So what?
Are we gonna do nothing?

1047
01:09:35.291 --> 01:09:36.333
[Gustavo] Roberto.

1048
01:09:38.333 --> 01:09:39.625
[sighs]

1049
01:09:43.125 --> 01:09:44.416
To survive, we gotta eat.

1050
01:09:47.041 --> 01:09:49.416
[all breathing shakily]

1051
01:09:56.666 --> 01:09:57.791
[Roberto sniffles]

1052
01:10:11.250 --> 01:10:12.666
[group crying]

1053
01:10:12.750 --> 01:10:14.958
[glass shard slicing]

1054
01:10:20.250 --> 01:10:21.375
[Numa sighs]

1055
01:10:23.666 --> 01:10:26.041
[flesh tearing]

1056
01:10:31.541 --> 01:10:33.291
[exhales shakily]

1057
01:10:34.375 --> 01:10:36.375
[crying softly]

1058
01:10:38.833 --> 01:10:40.833
[group breathing shakily]

1059
01:10:44.000 --> 01:10:45.708
Now you're letting yourselves die?

1060
01:10:50.375 --> 01:10:51.875
After all we've been through?

1061
01:11:00.375 --> 01:11:02.375
[somber music playing]

1062
01:11:14.833 --> 01:11:16.833
[chewing]

1063
01:11:27.833 --> 01:11:29.083
[Numa exhales sharply]

1064
01:11:29.166 --> 01:11:31.166
[crying]

1065
01:11:39.375 --> 01:11:41.541
[Numa grunting furiously]

1066
01:11:54.125 --> 01:11:56.541
We gotta get out. I'm not staying here!

1067
01:11:57.750 --> 01:11:59.333
We gotta get out!

1068
01:11:59.416 --> 01:12:01.208
[grunting]

1069
01:12:01.291 --> 01:12:02.541
[glass cracking]

1070
01:12:02.625 --> 01:12:04.833
[Numa] What else do you want?

1071
01:12:04.916 --> 01:12:06.208
Stop, Numa!

1072
01:12:06.291 --> 01:12:07.291
[Numa] Come on!

1073
01:12:08.166 --> 01:12:09.208
[Arturo] Stop it, Numa!

1074
01:12:09.291 --> 01:12:10.291
[screams]

1075
01:12:11.083 --> 01:12:12.500
- [inhales sharply]
- [Arturo] Numa!

1076
01:12:12.583 --> 01:12:14.083
[Numa groaning]

1077
01:12:21.500 --> 01:12:23.500
[panting]

1078
01:12:26.791 --> 01:12:32.541
{\an8}DAY 20
FOUR DAYS BURIED

1079
01:12:44.291 --> 01:12:45.291
[straining]

1080
01:12:52.958 --> 01:12:54.500
[gasps]

1081
01:12:54.583 --> 01:12:55.583
[mouthing]

1082
01:12:56.333 --> 01:12:59.291
- I see the sky!
- [bright string music playing]

1083
01:13:02.000 --> 01:13:03.791
Come on, Moncho. Go first. You're smaller.

1084
01:13:03.875 --> 01:13:06.208
Go. Go, go, go.

1085
01:13:09.375 --> 01:13:12.458
[grunts, yells]

1086
01:13:19.541 --> 01:13:22.250
[grunts]

1087
01:13:23.041 --> 01:13:24.291
The sun! [sighs]

1088
01:13:26.041 --> 01:13:27.875
Help me! Come on!

1089
01:13:27.958 --> 01:13:29.291
[panting]

1090
01:13:31.458 --> 01:13:32.583
[strains]

1091
01:13:35.500 --> 01:13:37.458
[panting]

1092
01:13:39.166 --> 01:13:43.041
[man 1 laughing, sighs]

1093
01:13:44.708 --> 01:13:46.875
[man 2 exclaims]

1094
01:13:51.583 --> 01:13:52.625
[sighs]

1095
01:13:53.958 --> 01:13:55.083
We made it.

1096
01:13:56.333 --> 01:13:59.208
[takes a deep breath]

1097
01:13:59.291 --> 01:14:01.875
Hey! What do you see?

1098
01:14:02.458 --> 01:14:04.208
Margarita's out here, Álvaro.

1099
01:14:04.291 --> 01:14:06.666
- Your girlfriend!
- [man 3] In a bikini!

1100
01:14:06.750 --> 01:14:08.958
[Álvaro] Tell her I'll be right up!
[chuckles]

1101
01:14:09.041 --> 01:14:12.208
- [man 4] We're alive!
- [man 5] We made it!

1102
01:14:12.291 --> 01:14:15.666
[survivors cheering and shouting]

1103
01:14:23.416 --> 01:14:24.500
[Coche] Hey! Come on!

1104
01:14:29.916 --> 01:14:32.666
[wind whipping]

1105
01:14:40.333 --> 01:14:42.166
[metal clangs]

1106
01:14:42.250 --> 01:14:46.208
[grunts] The bottle. The bottle.

1107
01:14:47.625 --> 01:14:49.625
[ominous string music playing]

1108
01:14:55.708 --> 01:14:57.708
[music fades]

1109
01:14:58.583 --> 01:15:00.166
[Arturo] <i>How's the leg?</i>

1110
01:15:00.250 --> 01:15:04.250
[sighs] It's okay.
It's just a cut. I'll be fine.

1111
01:15:04.333 --> 01:15:06.083
Save your energy, Numa.

1112
01:15:07.333 --> 01:15:08.833
'Cause I don't have any left.

1113
01:15:08.916 --> 01:15:10.750
[Numa] Don't say that, Arturo.

1114
01:15:13.416 --> 01:15:14.416
Don't lose your faith.

1115
01:15:15.500 --> 01:15:17.708
I have more faith
than I ever had in my whole life.

1116
01:15:17.791 --> 01:15:21.041
[chuckles] What, are you an altar boy now?

1117
01:15:21.125 --> 01:15:23.833
- [chuckles, coughs]
- [Arturo] Don't laugh at me.

1118
01:15:24.833 --> 01:15:25.958
[Roberto coughs]

1119
01:15:31.083 --> 01:15:32.416
'Cause my faith...

1120
01:15:34.125 --> 01:15:35.416
Sorry, Numa.

1121
01:15:36.875 --> 01:15:37.916
...isn't in your God.

1122
01:15:41.375 --> 01:15:42.625
Because that God

1123
01:15:44.208 --> 01:15:46.416
tells me what I'm supposed to do at home.

1124
01:15:48.583 --> 01:15:51.166
But he doesn't tell me
what to do on the mountain.

1125
01:15:52.291 --> 01:15:56.958
What's happening here
is a completely different situation.

1126
01:15:59.125 --> 01:16:00.125
Numa.

1127
01:16:01.083 --> 01:16:03.583
- [fuselage clangs]
- [Arturo] This is my heaven.

1128
01:16:04.250 --> 01:16:05.958
I believe in another god.

1129
01:16:08.291 --> 01:16:09.458
I believe

1130
01:16:10.791 --> 01:16:13.625
in the god that Roberto
keeps inside his head

1131
01:16:14.541 --> 01:16:16.791
when he comes to heal each of my wounds.

1132
01:16:20.291 --> 01:16:22.791
In the god that Nando keeps in his legs

1133
01:16:24.625 --> 01:16:27.125
and that lets him continue walking
no matter what.

1134
01:16:33.041 --> 01:16:34.916
I believe in Daniel's hands...

1135
01:16:37.000 --> 01:16:38.500
when he cuts the meat.

1136
01:16:40.750 --> 01:16:42.708
And Fito, when he gives it to us

1137
01:16:44.583 --> 01:16:47.208
without saying which of our friends
it belonged to.

1138
01:16:48.291 --> 01:16:50.125
That way, we can eat it without...

1139
01:16:54.208 --> 01:16:56.166
without having to remember their faces.

1140
01:17:00.291 --> 01:17:01.916
That's the god I believe in.

1141
01:17:04.666 --> 01:17:06.291
I believe in Roberto.

1142
01:17:07.958 --> 01:17:09.083
In Nando.

1143
01:17:12.041 --> 01:17:13.041
In Daniel.

1144
01:17:14.916 --> 01:17:16.208
In Fito.

1145
01:17:19.583 --> 01:17:21.250
And in our dead friends.

1146
01:17:23.208 --> 01:17:24.208
[sniffles]

1147
01:17:26.166 --> 01:17:28.125
You're a philosopher, Arturo.

1148
01:17:29.041 --> 01:17:30.333
[chuckles]

1149
01:17:30.916 --> 01:17:32.416
Altar boy and philosopher.

1150
01:17:33.333 --> 01:17:34.791
[sighs]

1151
01:17:46.291 --> 01:17:48.000
[Coche grunts]

1152
01:17:50.250 --> 01:17:51.250
[man 1] Okay.

1153
01:17:51.333 --> 01:17:53.208
- [man 2] Come on!
- [Nando] We have to go now.

1154
01:17:54.333 --> 01:17:56.666
- Look at the sun.
- [Roberto] We need to wait.

1155
01:17:57.166 --> 01:17:59.791
- [Nando] Wait for what?
- To be prepared.

1156
01:18:00.583 --> 01:18:02.333
What if we get caught in a storm?

1157
01:18:03.083 --> 01:18:04.875
We need temperatures to rise.

1158
01:18:04.958 --> 01:18:07.041
We can't spend a single night
out in the open.

1159
01:18:07.750 --> 01:18:08.958
Tell him, Numa.

1160
01:18:09.875 --> 01:18:11.583
[Pedro] The thaw starts on November 15th.

1161
01:18:11.666 --> 01:18:14.041
There's a lower risk of storms
because temperatures rise.

1162
01:18:14.125 --> 01:18:18.125
- [Nando] Two weeks... just waiting.
- No. Two weeks of preparation.

1163
01:18:19.333 --> 01:18:22.458
So far, we've always gone out
without a plan, and we've failed.

1164
01:18:23.166 --> 01:18:25.333
We don't even know
what kind of distance we're facing.

1165
01:18:26.208 --> 01:18:27.208
[Coche] Hey!

1166
01:18:28.208 --> 01:18:29.666
We need help over here!

1167
01:18:29.750 --> 01:18:32.375
- [man 3] Go grab those chairs!
- [Coche] Come on. Dig

1168
01:18:32.458 --> 01:18:33.500
[man 4] Come help.

1169
01:18:35.125 --> 01:18:37.708
[Coche] All good? Grab those plates.

1170
01:18:37.791 --> 01:18:40.041
- Yeah? Let's go.
- [man 5] Need help?

1171
01:18:40.125 --> 01:18:42.309
- [man 6] How can I help?
- [Coche] Dig on the other side.

1172
01:18:42.333 --> 01:18:44.708
[indistinct chatter]

1173
01:18:44.791 --> 01:18:47.291
[Roberto and Nando speaking indistinctly]

1174
01:18:55.666 --> 01:18:58.791
I don't get it.
I thought you didn't wanna die here.

1175
01:19:04.416 --> 01:19:09.583
DAY 34
THE THAW BEGINS

1176
01:19:11.250 --> 01:19:13.291
[water dripping]

1177
01:19:18.125 --> 01:19:21.208
Help me, Roberto. Give me a hand.

1178
01:19:21.291 --> 01:19:23.625
- [Arturo coughing]
- Watch it. Hold his head, please.

1179
01:19:23.708 --> 01:19:27.000
- Very slowly. Lift him. There you go.
- [Arturo groaning]

1180
01:19:27.083 --> 01:19:29.333
Slowly. Slowly. Slowly.

1181
01:19:30.208 --> 01:19:32.541
- Easy, easy, Arturo. That's it.
- [coughs weakly]

1182
01:19:32.625 --> 01:19:35.333
[Gustavo] Let's lift his shirt up slowly.
That's it.

1183
01:19:35.875 --> 01:19:37.291
[Arturo groans]

1184
01:19:40.833 --> 01:19:43.791
[coughs]

1185
01:19:43.875 --> 01:19:45.208
[Gustavo] <i>Arturo's really sick.</i>

1186
01:19:45.875 --> 01:19:48.916
He's got three days. Vasco, maybe five.

1187
01:19:49.583 --> 01:19:50.500
What do you think?

1188
01:19:50.583 --> 01:19:51.791
About what?

1189
01:19:52.291 --> 01:19:54.958
- The days they have left.
- What do you want, Gustavo?

1190
01:19:55.041 --> 01:19:57.083
- [guys shouting below]
- Say it.

1191
01:19:58.500 --> 01:19:59.500
What is it?

1192
01:20:02.291 --> 01:20:05.125
Roberto, there's nothing more
we can do here as doctors.

1193
01:20:06.750 --> 01:20:09.291
We're gonna end up becoming gravediggers.

1194
01:20:11.583 --> 01:20:13.208
Now, I know how hard it is.

1195
01:20:14.166 --> 01:20:16.416
But you're the strongest player
on the team.

1196
01:20:17.833 --> 01:20:19.666
Now you have to walk for everyone else.

1197
01:20:19.750 --> 01:20:21.500
[Roberto sighs]

1198
01:20:21.583 --> 01:20:23.583
[muffled panting]

1199
01:20:23.666 --> 01:20:26.416
[crowd cheering]

1200
01:20:26.500 --> 01:20:27.583
[echoing] Pass it!

1201
01:20:29.458 --> 01:20:30.916
Roberto, pass it!

1202
01:20:31.416 --> 01:20:34.125
- [group grunts]
- [Gustavo] Careful. Over there.

1203
01:20:34.208 --> 01:20:37.000
- [Arturo gasping for air]
- [Gustavo] Move him.

1204
01:20:40.708 --> 01:20:41.958
Let's put him here.

1205
01:20:50.041 --> 01:20:53.166
I'm here. I'm here. Breathe, Arturo.
Breathe with me. Come on.

1206
01:20:53.916 --> 01:20:56.666
[Numa] <i>Arturo Nogueira's lungs
are filled with fluid.</i>

1207
01:20:57.791 --> 01:20:58.916
<i>He can't hold on.</i>

1208
01:20:59.000 --> 01:21:01.875
[gently] There you go. There you go.

1209
01:21:01.958 --> 01:21:05.541
- [Numa] <i>Gustavo tries to help.</i>
- That's it. There you go. There you go.

1210
01:21:07.291 --> 01:21:08.811
[Numa] <i>But no one can breathe for him.</i>

1211
01:21:08.875 --> 01:21:11.833
[Gustavo] Good job. Good job.

1212
01:21:15.958 --> 01:21:20.083
- [wind howling outside]
- [Gustavo] There you go. There you go.

1213
01:21:46.250 --> 01:21:48.250
[foreboding instrumental music playing]

1214
01:21:56.416 --> 01:21:57.416
[Numa grunts]

1215
01:22:00.625 --> 01:22:02.208
[Numa] <i>We have to try everything.</i>

1216
01:22:11.125 --> 01:22:12.750
<i>Four of us volunteer.</i>

1217
01:22:16.333 --> 01:22:18.750
<i>We head downhill towards Argentina.</i>

1218
01:22:19.250 --> 01:22:23.208
{\an8}<i>With warmer clothes...
in the hope of surviving a night outside.</i>

1219
01:22:23.291 --> 01:22:24.958
{\an8}DAY 36
EXPEDITION EAST, ARGENTINA

1220
01:22:34.083 --> 01:22:36.083
[all panting]

1221
01:22:53.000 --> 01:22:54.333
[Numa grunts]

1222
01:22:56.000 --> 01:22:57.041
[moans]

1223
01:23:01.750 --> 01:23:02.750
[Nando] Numa!

1224
01:23:03.166 --> 01:23:05.166
[Numa wheezing]

1225
01:23:07.208 --> 01:23:08.375
[coughs weakly]

1226
01:23:11.583 --> 01:23:13.250
[groans] Ow.

1227
01:23:15.166 --> 01:23:17.625
[Roberto] Numa, you okay?

1228
01:23:18.500 --> 01:23:19.500
[Numa grunts]

1229
01:23:24.500 --> 01:23:25.500
[Roberto] It's infected.

1230
01:23:32.916 --> 01:23:34.083
Let's go back.

1231
01:23:35.875 --> 01:23:37.125
We can't carry him.

1232
01:23:39.958 --> 01:23:42.750
- [Nando] Roberto!
- I'm going back alone.

1233
01:23:47.750 --> 01:23:49.041
The plane's still close.

1234
01:23:55.708 --> 01:23:56.875
[Nando] Okay.

1235
01:24:02.041 --> 01:24:03.083
[Numa] Sorry.

1236
01:24:03.166 --> 01:24:06.250
[tense instrumental music playing]

1237
01:24:34.958 --> 01:24:37.958
- [distorted] What happened?
- Numa?

1238
01:24:38.041 --> 01:24:39.125
[echoing] Numa?

1239
01:24:39.208 --> 01:24:41.166
Where are the others?

1240
01:24:42.166 --> 01:24:43.958
Numa, answer me. Say something.

1241
01:24:44.041 --> 01:24:45.833
[Daniel] It's okay. We're here.

1242
01:24:45.916 --> 01:24:47.083
[Pancho] What happened?

1243
01:24:51.458 --> 01:24:53.291
- [music fades]
- [crying]

1244
01:24:53.375 --> 01:24:55.375
[Vasco] Where is he? My dad!

1245
01:24:55.458 --> 01:24:57.916
- [Daniel] No, Vasco. We're here.
- [Vasco] Dad?

1246
01:24:58.000 --> 01:25:00.101
- [Daniel] Calm down. We're here.
- [Vasco] Where's Dad?

1247
01:25:00.125 --> 01:25:03.291
[Daniel] Look at me.
Look at me. Your dad's here.

1248
01:25:03.791 --> 01:25:06.583
Look at me. We're here. We're here.

1249
01:25:06.666 --> 01:25:08.166
[Vasco continues sobbing]

1250
01:25:11.416 --> 01:25:13.791
- [Vasco] Dad! Dad, come here!
- Stop.

1251
01:25:16.291 --> 01:25:17.583
Calm down.

1252
01:25:18.708 --> 01:25:19.958
We're here.

1253
01:25:21.333 --> 01:25:22.666
[gently] Vasco.

1254
01:25:22.750 --> 01:25:24.375
- Hey, Vasco! Look at me!
- [Vasco] Dad!

1255
01:25:24.458 --> 01:25:27.500
[panting, sobs]

1256
01:25:28.291 --> 01:25:32.291
[announcer on PA] <i>Flight 328,
we are now boarding at gate ten.</i>

1257
01:25:32.375 --> 01:25:35.875
- Thanks.
- [Marcelo] Rafael... Rafael Echevarren.

1258
01:25:35.958 --> 01:25:37.375
Huh? <i>Echavarren</i>!

1259
01:25:37.458 --> 01:25:39.458
[somber instrumental music playing]

1260
01:25:44.041 --> 01:25:46.500
[crying softly]

1261
01:26:04.708 --> 01:26:06.291
[Numa] <i>I don't understand, Javier.</i>

1262
01:26:07.000 --> 01:26:09.541
From the very first moment
we crashed in this place,

1263
01:26:09.625 --> 01:26:11.666
I've tried to help as much as I could.

1264
01:26:13.666 --> 01:26:14.708
I tried...

1265
01:26:16.583 --> 01:26:18.666
to always do the right thing, you know?

1266
01:26:22.625 --> 01:26:24.750
And now, with my leg like this...

1267
01:26:28.791 --> 01:26:30.083
I'm useless.

1268
01:26:34.916 --> 01:26:36.500
What does it all mean?

1269
01:26:37.416 --> 01:26:39.708
What's the meaning of the death of Arturo?

1270
01:26:39.791 --> 01:26:43.375
The death of Vasco?
Or the death of everybody else?

1271
01:26:51.166 --> 01:26:53.916
Liliana gave everything. Always.

1272
01:26:55.916 --> 01:26:56.916
[sighs]

1273
01:26:58.291 --> 01:27:01.166
During the avalanche,
while buried under the snow,

1274
01:27:01.250 --> 01:27:03.708
I could feel her body underneath mine.

1275
01:27:08.208 --> 01:27:11.583
I remember there was only a few inches
between me and the surface.

1276
01:27:11.666 --> 01:27:13.958
I could actually pull my head out, and...

1277
01:27:14.041 --> 01:27:16.625
and shout at her
with all my strength I had.

1278
01:27:16.708 --> 01:27:18.541
"Liliana, hold on!"

1279
01:27:18.625 --> 01:27:20.541
"I'll get you out. I'm alive, love."

1280
01:27:21.791 --> 01:27:23.583
I saw them stepping over where she was,

1281
01:27:23.666 --> 01:27:27.208
and I shouted, "Oh, my God!
Don't step on her! Don't!"

1282
01:27:27.291 --> 01:27:30.083
"Don't step on her, please!
Liliana's trapped below."

1283
01:27:30.583 --> 01:27:31.958
[sighs deeply]

1284
01:27:33.000 --> 01:27:36.666
But there was simply no way to get her out
if I didn't get out first.

1285
01:27:39.000 --> 01:27:43.208
But I was unable to move because my feet
were pressed against her chest.

1286
01:27:45.208 --> 01:27:49.166
And if I pushed against her,
it would make her sink deeper and deeper.

1287
01:27:55.208 --> 01:27:57.291
What is the meaning of that, Numa?

1288
01:28:02.041 --> 01:28:07.208
[scoffs] When we finally got to Liliana,
she was just a lifeless corpse.

1289
01:28:07.916 --> 01:28:10.541
At that moment,
as they kept digging up friends,

1290
01:28:10.625 --> 01:28:13.666
one dead, one alive, one dead, one alive...

1291
01:28:14.500 --> 01:28:19.208
then... I hugged Liliana
with all my strength.

1292
01:28:20.791 --> 01:28:24.041
And I felt a love
I'd never felt in my life.

1293
01:28:24.125 --> 01:28:26.125
[gentle instrumental music playing]

1294
01:28:31.291 --> 01:28:33.500
And I realized that I had a purpose,

1295
01:28:35.291 --> 01:28:39.500
which was to take that love that
I was squeezing there against my chest...

1296
01:28:41.250 --> 01:28:43.458
and bring it to my kids back home.

1297
01:28:47.041 --> 01:28:48.916
Her death was not in vain.

1298
01:28:53.791 --> 01:28:55.750
That wound doesn't make you useless.

1299
01:29:05.458 --> 01:29:07.583
[inhales sharply, groans]

1300
01:29:13.416 --> 01:29:15.416
[icy wind howling]

1301
01:29:23.125 --> 01:29:25.166
[music fades]

1302
01:29:27.333 --> 01:29:29.333
[panting]

1303
01:29:32.916 --> 01:29:34.596
[Roberto] Someone ripped
all the parts off.

1304
01:29:35.833 --> 01:29:37.851
- [Roy] Are you serious?
- [Roberto] Are you helping?

1305
01:29:37.875 --> 01:29:39.166
[quietly] Nando?

1306
01:29:40.250 --> 01:29:41.875
They told me you've got lazy.

1307
01:29:42.375 --> 01:29:45.166
That you sleep all day. Why?

1308
01:29:46.125 --> 01:29:48.666
- You need to train, Numa.
- Why are you here?

1309
01:29:49.416 --> 01:29:51.041
You're not gonna believe this.

1310
01:29:51.833 --> 01:29:55.458
We walked for about
two, three hours, towards the east.

1311
01:29:57.291 --> 01:30:00.958
<i>Until, suddenly,
behind a hill, we found the tail.</i>

1312
01:30:02.500 --> 01:30:04.208
I can't believe we found it.

1313
01:30:05.541 --> 01:30:07.500
It... it catapulted itself forward.

1314
01:30:09.250 --> 01:30:10.250
To the other side.

1315
01:30:11.125 --> 01:30:12.333
It was amazing.

1316
01:30:12.833 --> 01:30:15.500
It was completely full
of scattered suitcases, clean coats.

1317
01:30:16.375 --> 01:30:18.000
<i>We found bottles of rum.</i>

1318
01:30:19.250 --> 01:30:20.750
<i>Cigarettes.</i>

1319
01:30:24.750 --> 01:30:25.916
[softly] And chocolate.

1320
01:30:26.000 --> 01:30:27.250
[Numa inhales shakily]

1321
01:30:31.541 --> 01:30:33.916
Stop, stop, stop, stop. Not the wrapper.

1322
01:30:34.416 --> 01:30:35.791
[clicks tongue]

1323
01:30:35.875 --> 01:30:39.791
Now you're telling me
what to eat, man? [coughs]

1324
01:30:40.625 --> 01:30:41.625
There you go.

1325
01:30:42.500 --> 01:30:43.583
Mm!

1326
01:30:44.666 --> 01:30:46.375
[moans]

1327
01:30:49.500 --> 01:30:51.000
[Nando] You were right, Numa.

1328
01:30:51.083 --> 01:30:55.666
We spent a night out in the open,
and we almost didn't make it.

1329
01:30:58.958 --> 01:31:01.041
<i>But we found the plane's batteries.</i>

1330
01:31:01.666 --> 01:31:03.750
- [electricity crackles]
- [gasps]

1331
01:31:03.833 --> 01:31:05.291
[Nando] <i>They were in the tail.</i>

1332
01:31:10.125 --> 01:31:12.250
It'll be much easier
to bring the radio here.

1333
01:31:14.541 --> 01:31:16.458
Did you see Roy fixed the portable radio?

1334
01:31:16.541 --> 01:31:19.458
And Roberto thinks he can get
that one in the plane to work too.

1335
01:31:21.333 --> 01:31:23.083
We're going back down there.

1336
01:31:24.125 --> 01:31:25.333
We need to try.

1337
01:31:43.041 --> 01:31:45.041
[energetic string music playing]

1338
01:31:50.125 --> 01:31:54.000
[Numa] <i>Nando, Roberto and Tintín leave
with Roy towards the tail of the plane.</i>

1339
01:31:58.666 --> 01:32:00.333
<i>I wish I could go with them.</i>

1340
01:32:04.916 --> 01:32:07.666
<i>Roy is weak and doesn't think
the radio will work.</i>

1341
01:32:07.750 --> 01:32:10.083
Come on, Roy. Not a lot of time.

1342
01:32:10.666 --> 01:32:12.083
[Numa] <i>He's terrified.</i>

1343
01:32:13.625 --> 01:32:15.291
<i>But he's doing it for the team.</i>

1344
01:32:24.833 --> 01:32:28.000
- [chuckles] I don't believe it.
- [Roberto] Nice, Roy.

1345
01:32:37.208 --> 01:32:40.000
- 1-C-6-0-1.
- Which one is it?

1346
01:32:40.083 --> 01:32:42.541
B... Not this one. What was it?

1347
01:32:42.625 --> 01:32:43.708
Uh...

1348
01:32:44.500 --> 01:32:46.000
- One, seven.
- [Roy] Seven...

1349
01:32:46.083 --> 01:32:47.166
What if it doesn't work?

1350
01:32:48.416 --> 01:32:49.416
Huh?

1351
01:32:49.791 --> 01:32:51.083
What do we do?

1352
01:32:51.166 --> 01:32:52.833
I guess we start walking back.

1353
01:32:54.500 --> 01:32:55.500
Right, Roberto?

1354
01:32:56.208 --> 01:32:58.250
Toward the west. To Chile.

1355
01:32:59.708 --> 01:33:01.166
[static crackles on radio]

1356
01:33:02.416 --> 01:33:03.541
[Roberto] Hello?

1357
01:33:05.583 --> 01:33:06.458
Hello?

1358
01:33:06.541 --> 01:33:08.083
[indistinct radio chatter]

1359
01:33:08.166 --> 01:33:10.708
We're the Uruguayans
who crash-landed in the Andes.

1360
01:33:10.791 --> 01:33:13.333
Can you hear me? We're still here!

1361
01:33:14.333 --> 01:33:15.333
Hello?

1362
01:33:20.083 --> 01:33:20.916
Hello?

1363
01:33:21.000 --> 01:33:22.375
[static crackles on radio]

1364
01:33:22.458 --> 01:33:24.458
[tango music playing on radio]

1365
01:33:24.541 --> 01:33:27.250
[indistinct chatter]

1366
01:33:28.958 --> 01:33:31.083
[man] Uh, I don't know. I never tried it.

1367
01:33:31.583 --> 01:33:34.833
- ["Zamba del riego" playing on radio]
- [Numa sighs]

1368
01:33:36.416 --> 01:33:39.958
[Numa] <i>With every day that passes,
we lose more of our strength.</i>

1369
01:33:44.583 --> 01:33:46.708
- [Numa sighs]
- [Pancho] It's okay.

1370
01:33:46.791 --> 01:33:50.625
[Numa] <i>The food rations aren't enough,
so we strip the bones of meat.</i>

1371
01:33:51.125 --> 01:33:52.291
[news broadcast on radio]

1372
01:33:52.375 --> 01:33:56.375
[Numa] <i>What was once unthinkable
became routine.</i>

1373
01:33:56.458 --> 01:33:58.791
[reporter] <i>...number
of intercontinental ballistic missiles</i>

1374
01:33:58.875 --> 01:34:00.500
<i>and other strategic offensive arms.</i>

1375
01:34:00.583 --> 01:34:02.333
[Numa] <i>We just stopped caring.</i>

1376
01:34:05.375 --> 01:34:06.375
[Pancho] Come on.

1377
01:34:07.916 --> 01:34:09.416
Here. Eat a little.

1378
01:34:11.875 --> 01:34:13.000
You have to eat, Numa.

1379
01:34:28.750 --> 01:34:29.750
Half and half.

1380
01:34:32.583 --> 01:34:33.625
You can't give up now.

1381
01:34:34.416 --> 01:34:36.416
No, I'm not givin' up, Pancho.

1382
01:34:37.500 --> 01:34:38.750
You know, I'm dying.

1383
01:34:46.333 --> 01:34:47.458
And it hurts me to not...

1384
01:34:49.083 --> 01:34:50.791
not be able to do more for you.

1385
01:34:50.875 --> 01:34:52.250
Don't say that.

1386
01:34:53.750 --> 01:34:55.000
Think of yourself.

1387
01:34:57.083 --> 01:34:58.750
You want me to think of myself?

1388
01:35:02.416 --> 01:35:03.625
Look at me.

1389
01:35:03.708 --> 01:35:05.958
I'm 25 years old, Pancho.

1390
01:35:06.916 --> 01:35:10.333
I've got my enitre life ahead.
I've got everything left to do.

1391
01:35:11.625 --> 01:35:15.250
I want to... see my siblings again.

1392
01:35:15.333 --> 01:35:17.125
See my mother, my father.

1393
01:35:17.916 --> 01:35:19.291
- I want to dance.
- [scoffs]

1394
01:35:19.375 --> 01:35:21.333
- Numa, you don't dance.
- I know.

1395
01:35:23.041 --> 01:35:24.208
But now I want to.

1396
01:35:25.333 --> 01:35:27.083
I wanna do it all, Pancho.

1397
01:35:29.291 --> 01:35:30.291
I want to laugh.

1398
01:35:30.375 --> 01:35:33.000
- I want to cry.
- Then cry.

1399
01:35:33.083 --> 01:35:34.541
- I can't.
- Cry.

1400
01:35:35.750 --> 01:35:38.375
Do it. Come on, cry.

1401
01:35:39.125 --> 01:35:40.166
Just cry with me.

1402
01:35:41.083 --> 01:35:42.791
- [laughs]
- What's so funny?

1403
01:35:42.875 --> 01:35:44.375
[chuckles]

1404
01:35:44.458 --> 01:35:47.166
Cry with me. Come on. Let it go.

1405
01:35:47.250 --> 01:35:49.875
[both crying]

1406
01:35:51.833 --> 01:35:53.125
Do it, moron.

1407
01:35:54.958 --> 01:35:56.083
Come on.

1408
01:36:04.791 --> 01:36:07.291
[sobbing softly]

1409
01:36:07.375 --> 01:36:08.708
[metal clatters]

1410
01:36:21.625 --> 01:36:22.833
[Tintín] Nando!

1411
01:36:22.916 --> 01:36:23.958
Look at this.

1412
01:36:29.500 --> 01:36:31.750
- What's that?
- It's waterproof.

1413
01:36:32.375 --> 01:36:33.708
We can use it, yeah?

1414
01:36:34.916 --> 01:36:36.708
It was covering some pipes.

1415
01:36:36.791 --> 01:36:38.958
- Is there more?
- [Tintín] Yeah. There's a lot.

1416
01:36:39.041 --> 01:36:41.750
[Roberto] Two, four... One, C.

1417
01:36:44.666 --> 01:36:47.541
- [electricity crackles]
- [Roberto gasps]

1418
01:36:51.583 --> 01:36:53.166
[screams]

1419
01:36:53.250 --> 01:36:55.500
No! [grunting]

1420
01:36:55.583 --> 01:36:58.166
[groans, sobbing]

1421
01:37:00.333 --> 01:37:07.083
AS OF TODAY, NOVEMBER 29, 1972,
THERE ARE 17 MORE SURVIVORS UP ABOVE

1422
01:37:07.166 --> 01:37:11.166
IN THE URUGUAYAN PLANE
THAT CRASHED IN THE MOUNTAINS

1423
01:37:16.750 --> 01:37:19.333
[group panting]

1424
01:37:27.000 --> 01:37:28.041
[man] What happened?

1425
01:37:29.875 --> 01:37:31.250
[Roberto] The radio didn't work.

1426
01:37:32.625 --> 01:37:34.458
[Tintín] But we found this fabric there.

1427
01:37:35.208 --> 01:37:38.000
- [Daniel] What's this?
- [Tintín] It's waterproof.

1428
01:37:39.125 --> 01:37:42.416
- We can make a vest.
- [Roberto] No. Not a vest, Tintín.

1429
01:37:42.500 --> 01:37:43.791
Let's make a sleeping bag.

1430
01:37:43.875 --> 01:37:47.750
With a sleeping bag, we could get
through the night. There's enough fabric.

1431
01:37:49.291 --> 01:37:50.791
Or we could make a big one.

1432
01:37:52.166 --> 01:37:53.646
[Nando] When are we leaving, Roberto?

1433
01:37:55.541 --> 01:37:56.708
[panting]

1434
01:38:00.791 --> 01:38:01.791
Roberto.

1435
01:38:02.916 --> 01:38:03.916
When?

1436
01:38:06.541 --> 01:38:08.208
As soon as the sleeping bag is done.

1437
01:38:08.291 --> 01:38:10.375
[reporter on radio]
<i>58 days after the disappearance</i>

1438
01:38:10.458 --> 01:38:14.416
<i>of the Fairchild 571 aircraft
from the Uruguayan Air Force</i>

1439
01:38:14.500 --> 01:38:17.333
<i>with 40 passengers and five crew members</i>

1440
01:38:17.416 --> 01:38:20.666
<i>chartered to transport a rugby team
from the Old Christians Club</i>

1441
01:38:20.750 --> 01:38:22.958
<i>and their companions to Chile.</i>

1442
01:38:23.041 --> 01:38:27.166
<i>The local Air Force has specially equipped
a C-47 aircraft</i>

1443
01:38:27.250 --> 01:38:30.458
<i>to resume the search
in the Andean Mountain Range.</i>

1444
01:38:31.708 --> 01:38:35.250
[Nando] Come on, Roberto.
We can't go back to the beginning.

1445
01:38:35.750 --> 01:38:37.708
[Roberto] They said they'll look for us.

1446
01:38:37.791 --> 01:38:41.291
Those morons who flew right over
and... and didn't see us?

1447
01:38:41.375 --> 01:38:43.041
They're looking for bodies.

1448
01:38:43.125 --> 01:38:46.250
- We've been lost here for two months.
- [Nando] Two months, Roberto.

1449
01:38:46.333 --> 01:38:48.583
Do you still believe
they think we're alive?

1450
01:38:48.666 --> 01:38:51.291
- Well, we <i>are</i> alive.
- [Nando] Alive?

1451
01:38:51.375 --> 01:38:54.416
Just look at us. Look at this.

1452
01:38:55.000 --> 01:38:56.458
This isn't being alive.

1453
01:38:56.541 --> 01:38:58.708
We won't make it
just by praying, you know.

1454
01:38:59.208 --> 01:39:01.666
So you want to climb the mountain
sleeping in this?

1455
01:39:08.500 --> 01:39:10.041
[Fito] What are you doing, Roberto?

1456
01:39:10.625 --> 01:39:12.916
- Stop!
- [Nando] Roberto.

1457
01:39:13.416 --> 01:39:14.666
[Carlitos] You didn't like it?

1458
01:39:15.916 --> 01:39:19.166
[gentle instrumental music playing]

1459
01:39:46.250 --> 01:39:47.791
[bird calls]

1460
01:39:51.000 --> 01:39:53.541
[man whistling]

1461
01:39:54.958 --> 01:39:56.250
[whistling echoes]

1462
01:39:59.583 --> 01:40:00.958
[whistles]

1463
01:40:01.750 --> 01:40:03.291
[imitating birdsong]

1464
01:40:08.666 --> 01:40:12.041
[imitating owl hooting]

1465
01:40:13.708 --> 01:40:15.416
[clicks tongue]

1466
01:40:15.500 --> 01:40:17.041
[whistling continues]

1467
01:40:17.125 --> 01:40:20.625
- [imitates birdsong]
- [imitates dove cooing]

1468
01:40:20.708 --> 01:40:23.958
- [group imitating birds]
- [all laugh]

1469
01:40:26.125 --> 01:40:27.125
[Tintín] Guys.

1470
01:40:28.083 --> 01:40:29.625
I'm gonna take a picture.

1471
01:40:32.625 --> 01:40:35.625
- [camera shutter clicks]
- [somber music playing]

1472
01:40:38.000 --> 01:40:39.666
[camera shutter clicks]

1473
01:40:42.750 --> 01:40:44.000
[sighs]

1474
01:40:47.208 --> 01:40:48.333
[camera shutter clicks]

1475
01:40:48.416 --> 01:40:50.833
[Numa] <i>Tintín insists on taking pictures.</i>

1476
01:40:53.583 --> 01:40:57.375
<i>Like he's capturing memories of a trip
that he's comin' back from.</i>

1477
01:41:00.166 --> 01:41:01.958
<i>I wonder who these pictures are for.</i>

1478
01:41:02.541 --> 01:41:03.833
[camera shutter clicks]

1479
01:41:03.916 --> 01:41:04.916
[Numa] <i>For us?</i>

1480
01:41:05.500 --> 01:41:07.208
Smile, asshole.

1481
01:41:07.291 --> 01:41:08.958
[Numa] <i>I'll never see them.</i>

1482
01:41:09.041 --> 01:41:10.666
Come on. We can still smile.

1483
01:41:13.750 --> 01:41:15.750
<i>Maybe they're for our families.</i>

1484
01:41:15.833 --> 01:41:18.958
<i>Or for other people
who are remembering us now,</i>

1485
01:41:19.041 --> 01:41:22.000
<i>looking at pictures of us
that were taken in the past.</i>

1486
01:41:22.083 --> 01:41:23.500
[Tintín] Carlos. Look at me!

1487
01:41:24.541 --> 01:41:29.291
[Numa] <i>And when they look at them,
we'll live again in their imaginations.</i>

1488
01:41:29.791 --> 01:41:33.791
<i>Because they'll ask themselves
the same questions we're asking.</i>

1489
01:41:36.958 --> 01:41:39.291
- [camera shutter clicks]
<i>- "What happened to them?"</i>

1490
01:41:40.416 --> 01:41:43.000
- [camera shutter clicks]
- [Numa] <i>What happened to us?</i>

1491
01:41:45.791 --> 01:41:47.666
<i>Who were we on the mountain?</i>

1492
01:41:49.583 --> 01:41:50.583
[Numa] <i>Nando.</i>

1493
01:41:51.875 --> 01:41:56.875
I want you to know that
you have my permission to use my body.

1494
01:41:59.333 --> 01:42:01.500
Stop fucking around. Don't say that.

1495
01:42:03.833 --> 01:42:05.666
I'm know I'm not coming back.

1496
01:42:09.583 --> 01:42:10.708
Don't say that.

1497
01:42:12.208 --> 01:42:13.500
It's the truth.

1498
01:42:15.875 --> 01:42:18.041
[takes a deep breath]

1499
01:42:18.125 --> 01:42:19.375
But it's all right.

1500
01:42:20.333 --> 01:42:22.000
It's fine. I'm at peace.

1501
01:42:27.541 --> 01:42:29.583
I'm prepared for what's coming.

1502
01:42:31.666 --> 01:42:33.458
We both are, my brother.

1503
01:42:35.500 --> 01:42:40.666
And I'm so happy
to know that you guys are gonna make it.

1504
01:42:44.500 --> 01:42:46.875
That makes me feel very happy, Nando.

1505
01:42:49.041 --> 01:42:50.250
[exhales shakily]

1506
01:42:51.791 --> 01:42:53.666
[somber music continues]

1507
01:43:06.833 --> 01:43:08.833
[wind whistling outside]

1508
01:43:17.666 --> 01:43:18.791
[Numa exhales]

1509
01:43:39.416 --> 01:43:40.583
[weakly] Thank you.

1510
01:43:53.791 --> 01:43:55.791
{\an8}[somber choral music playing]

1511
01:43:58.458 --> 01:43:59.875
[Numa] <i>My name is Numa.</i>

1512
01:44:01.541 --> 01:44:04.833
<i>I died on December 11, 1972.</i>

1513
01:44:06.666 --> 01:44:07.916
<i>In my sleep.</i>

1514
01:45:15.875 --> 01:45:22.375
THERE IS NO GREATER LOVE
THAN TO GIVE ONE'S LIFE FOR FRIENDS

1515
01:45:24.250 --> 01:45:25.666
We're leaving tomorrow.

1516
01:45:25.750 --> 01:45:27.916
[music fades]

1517
01:45:28.000 --> 01:45:30.000
[energetic, rhythmic music playing]

1518
01:45:38.791 --> 01:45:40.000
[Coche] You got this.

1519
01:45:40.875 --> 01:45:42.684
- [Carlitos] Best of luck, Roberto.
- Thank you.

1520
01:45:42.708 --> 01:45:43.708
- Take care.
- You too.

1521
01:45:43.791 --> 01:45:44.916
[Carlitos] Keep going.

1522
01:45:45.875 --> 01:45:47.916
- No matter what.
- [man 1] My friend.

1523
01:45:48.541 --> 01:45:51.833
- Give me one more. [grunts]
- [Coche] Take care.

1524
01:45:59.375 --> 01:46:00.583
[Nando] Carlitos.

1525
01:46:01.583 --> 01:46:02.583
Yeah?

1526
01:46:04.250 --> 01:46:07.458
You can use the bodies
of my mom and Susy. Okay?

1527
01:46:08.625 --> 01:46:09.708
[man 2] Let's go!

1528
01:46:09.791 --> 01:46:12.416
- [man 3] Yeah, yeah!
- [man 2] You can do it!

1529
01:46:12.500 --> 01:46:14.166
- You got this!
- [Javier] Good luck!

1530
01:46:14.750 --> 01:46:17.458
[Carlitos] Come on, guys!
Look both ways before crossing

1531
01:46:17.541 --> 01:46:19.416
and don't forget about us afterwards!

1532
01:46:19.500 --> 01:46:22.208
- [man 3] We'll be waiting for you guys!
- We'll see you guys soon!

1533
01:46:22.291 --> 01:46:24.666
- [man 4] You can do it!
- [man 2] Come on, guys!

1534
01:46:28.916 --> 01:46:30.916
[energetic, rhythmic music building]

1535
01:46:49.000 --> 01:46:53.125
{\an8}DAY 61
EXPEDITION WEST, CHILE

1536
01:46:58.291 --> 01:47:00.291
[panting]

1537
01:47:08.791 --> 01:47:10.166
[sighs]

1538
01:47:10.250 --> 01:47:11.750
[Roberto] Nando!

1539
01:47:11.833 --> 01:47:15.000
We have to find a ledge
to put the sleeping bag on!

1540
01:47:16.291 --> 01:47:18.208
[Nando] We have to climb a little more!

1541
01:47:18.291 --> 01:47:20.458
We're not gonna make it up there!

1542
01:47:28.708 --> 01:47:29.708
I'll be in the middle.

1543
01:47:34.916 --> 01:47:36.916
[wind howling]

1544
01:48:01.250 --> 01:48:02.250
[Nando grunts]

1545
01:48:16.875 --> 01:48:18.875
[panting]

1546
01:48:37.750 --> 01:48:39.750
[breathing heavily]

1547
01:48:48.125 --> 01:48:50.375
[energetic music fades]

1548
01:48:50.458 --> 01:48:53.625
[ominous orchestral music playing]

1549
01:49:14.041 --> 01:49:16.750
[music fades slowly]

1550
01:49:16.833 --> 01:49:18.833
[wind gusting]

1551
01:49:50.750 --> 01:49:52.750
[panting]

1552
01:50:01.583 --> 01:50:03.041
It's so beautiful.

1553
01:50:10.541 --> 01:50:12.166
It's too bad we're dead.

1554
01:50:15.291 --> 01:50:16.500
I'm not going back.

1555
01:50:17.375 --> 01:50:21.916
The Andes have to end at some point
The snow too.

1556
01:50:22.875 --> 01:50:24.750
The sea's right behind there.

1557
01:50:26.250 --> 01:50:28.708
- This never ends.
- Look where we are, Roberto.

1558
01:50:30.000 --> 01:50:31.416
After all we've climbed.

1559
01:50:33.291 --> 01:50:34.750
We're so close now. Look.

1560
01:50:36.291 --> 01:50:39.875
We just need to cross the valley.
How long can it take?

1561
01:50:40.833 --> 01:50:42.166
Ten, twelve days?

1562
01:50:44.416 --> 01:50:46.250
We only have enough food for a week.

1563
01:50:47.500 --> 01:50:48.958
What do you want to do?

1564
01:50:49.791 --> 01:50:51.041
Come and walk with me...

1565
01:50:53.166 --> 01:50:54.541
or wait on the plane?

1566
01:50:57.833 --> 01:50:59.416
You're asking me to die with you.

1567
01:50:59.500 --> 01:51:01.375
I'm asking you to come with me.

1568
01:51:02.916 --> 01:51:06.000
Look. Look over there.
See those two peaks?

1569
01:51:06.083 --> 01:51:08.500
In the middle, like a pair of titties.

1570
01:51:09.875 --> 01:51:11.250
There's no snow there.

1571
01:51:12.791 --> 01:51:15.166
Can you see it? That's Chile.

1572
01:51:17.583 --> 01:51:18.583
Can you see it?

1573
01:51:29.750 --> 01:51:30.750
I do.

1574
01:51:31.750 --> 01:51:32.750
[Nando] Thanks.

1575
01:51:33.833 --> 01:51:35.000
Careful.

1576
01:51:35.083 --> 01:51:37.083
[Tintín panting]

1577
01:51:40.500 --> 01:51:44.083
[Tintín] <i>Nando and Roberto went on,
heading west.</i>

1578
01:51:45.750 --> 01:51:49.333
<i>We agreed I should come back
so the food would last longer.</i>

1579
01:51:52.833 --> 01:51:55.291
From above, you can actually see
some lower ridges.

1580
01:51:55.375 --> 01:51:57.458
Looks like they have
a sort of brownish color.

1581
01:52:00.250 --> 01:52:02.000
Like there's no more snow there.

1582
01:52:05.416 --> 01:52:07.750
The guys are healthy. Doing really great.

1583
01:52:07.833 --> 01:52:09.916
They have enough food for like ten days.

1584
01:52:10.916 --> 01:52:12.416
Nothing's gonna stop them.

1585
01:52:22.250 --> 01:52:24.250
[energetic, rhythmic music playing]

1586
01:52:44.666 --> 01:52:46.666
[panting]

1587
01:53:42.708 --> 01:53:43.708
A valley.

1588
01:53:43.791 --> 01:53:45.333
[takes a deep breath]

1589
01:53:48.375 --> 01:53:50.375
[music swells]

1590
01:54:08.625 --> 01:54:09.791
[birds singing]

1591
01:54:19.916 --> 01:54:21.916
[both panting]

1592
01:54:46.083 --> 01:54:48.083
[crickets chirping]

1593
01:54:55.083 --> 01:54:56.333
[sniffs]

1594
01:55:05.500 --> 01:55:07.250
[retches, coughs]

1595
01:55:11.625 --> 01:55:13.625
[gasping]

1596
01:55:31.541 --> 01:55:33.166
[coughs]

1597
01:55:46.416 --> 01:55:47.416
Roberto!

1598
01:55:50.166 --> 01:55:51.166
Roberto!

1599
01:55:52.416 --> 01:55:53.458
Nando!

1600
01:55:55.458 --> 01:55:57.666
[bright instrumental music playing]

1601
01:55:57.750 --> 01:55:59.291
Hey! Hey!

1602
01:55:59.375 --> 01:56:00.875
Hey! Help us, please!

1603
01:56:01.625 --> 01:56:04.125
We're from a plane
that crashed in the mountains!

1604
01:56:04.208 --> 01:56:07.333
- [Roberto] Hey! Hey!
- [Nando] Help us! We're starving!

1605
01:56:12.375 --> 01:56:15.000
AIR RESCUE SERVICE

1606
01:56:25.000 --> 01:56:26.791
{\an8}I'M FROM A PLANE

1607
01:56:26.875 --> 01:56:29.791
{\an8}[Numa] <i>"I'm from a plane
that crashed in the mountains."</i>

1608
01:56:29.875 --> 01:56:30.875
<i>"I'm Uruguayan."</i>

1609
01:56:33.625 --> 01:56:36.125
<i>"We've been walking
through the snow for ten days."</i>

1610
01:56:36.208 --> 01:56:39.083
<i>"There are 14 injured
and stranded people in the plane."</i>

1611
01:56:40.083 --> 01:56:42.916
<i>"We need to get out of here fast,
and we don't know how."</i>

1612
01:56:43.000 --> 01:56:44.125
Call from San Fernando.

1613
01:56:44.208 --> 01:56:46.666
- [Nando grunts]
- [Numa] <i>"We have no food."</i>

1614
01:56:47.166 --> 01:56:48.541
<i>"We are very weak."</i>

1615
01:56:49.541 --> 01:56:52.261
<i>- "When are you coming to get us?"</i>
- "When are you coming to get us?"

1616
01:56:52.333 --> 01:56:55.041
[Numa and man]
<i>"Please. We can barely walk."</i>

1617
01:56:55.125 --> 01:56:56.125
[Numa] <i>"Where are we?"</i>

1618
01:57:00.250 --> 01:57:01.166
[music stops]

1619
01:57:01.250 --> 01:57:02.958
[woman whispers] A call from San Fernando.

1620
01:57:12.916 --> 01:57:14.916
[chickens clucking]

1621
01:57:21.541 --> 01:57:22.666
[Nando] Mm.

1622
01:57:27.333 --> 01:57:28.416
[chuckles]

1623
01:57:29.166 --> 01:57:30.500
[horse neighs]

1624
01:57:30.583 --> 01:57:32.750
[chickens clucking]

1625
01:57:32.833 --> 01:57:34.458
[horses snort]

1626
01:57:36.791 --> 01:57:38.791
[horse whinnies]

1627
01:57:42.458 --> 01:57:44.875
[crowd clamoring]

1628
01:57:52.291 --> 01:57:54.267
- [reporter 1] Come on.
- [reporter 2] Camera ready?

1629
01:57:54.291 --> 01:57:56.351
- Get ready.
- [reporter 3] Let's talk to these guys.

1630
01:57:56.375 --> 01:57:58.375
[static crackling on radio]

1631
01:57:59.750 --> 01:58:03.833
[woman singing "Ave Maria" on radio]

1632
01:58:03.916 --> 01:58:05.916
[shivering]

1633
01:58:31.125 --> 01:58:33.525
[reporter] <i>We interrupt this broadcast,
ladies and gentlemen,</i>

1634
01:58:33.583 --> 01:58:37.166
<i>to bring you more information
on the news we gave you a few minutes ago.</i>

1635
01:58:37.250 --> 01:58:39.583
<i>We now have the names
of the two young survivors</i>

1636
01:58:39.666 --> 01:58:43.833
<i>from the Uruguayan plane that crashed
in the Andes 71 days ago.</i>

1637
01:58:43.916 --> 01:58:48.250
<i>Their names are Roberto Canessa
and Fernando Parrado.</i>

1638
01:58:48.333 --> 01:58:50.333
[helicopter blades whirring]

1639
01:58:51.875 --> 01:58:53.166
{\an8}CHILEAN AIR FORCE

1640
01:58:53.250 --> 01:58:58.333
{\an8}DAY 71
DECEMBER 22, 1972

1641
01:58:58.416 --> 01:59:00.416
[soothing orchestral music playing]

1642
01:59:08.625 --> 01:59:10.791
Pass it. Pass it to me.

1643
01:59:13.583 --> 01:59:14.708
[spits]

1644
01:59:28.416 --> 01:59:30.708
Lookin' good, huh? [chuckles]

1645
01:59:31.500 --> 01:59:32.541
[grunts]

1646
01:59:45.583 --> 01:59:47.375
What should we do with all this?

1647
02:00:21.875 --> 02:00:23.875
- [water running]
- [birds singing]

1648
02:00:38.125 --> 02:00:40.625
[phone ringing]

1649
02:00:40.708 --> 02:00:42.291
[man 1] <i>Okay, everyone.</i>

1650
02:00:42.375 --> 02:00:44.875
<i>I'm going to tell you
the names of the boys.</i>

1651
02:00:44.958 --> 02:00:46.642
<i>- Can you hear me?</i>
- [man 2] <i>Loud and clear.</i>

1652
02:00:46.666 --> 02:00:48.916
<i>Just repeat each
of the names twice, please.</i>

1653
02:00:50.083 --> 02:00:51.666
<i>Each name twice.</i>

1654
02:00:54.875 --> 02:00:56.583
[man 1] <i>Roberto Canessa.</i>

1655
02:00:57.833 --> 02:00:59.333
Roberto Canessa.

1656
02:00:59.833 --> 02:01:01.750
<i>Gustavo Zerbino.</i>

1657
02:01:02.416 --> 02:01:03.416
<i>Gustavo Zerbino.</i>

1658
02:01:04.625 --> 02:01:06.000
<i>Eduardo Strauch.</i>

1659
02:01:07.166 --> 02:01:08.333
<i>Eduardo Strauch.</i>

1660
02:01:09.333 --> 02:01:10.916
<i>Álvaro Mangino.</i>

1661
02:01:11.500 --> 02:01:13.041
<i>Álvaro Mangino.</i>

1662
02:01:13.875 --> 02:01:15.416
<i>Fernando Parrado.</i>

1663
02:01:16.208 --> 02:01:17.250
<i>Fernando Parrado.</i>

1664
02:01:18.416 --> 02:01:20.125
Antonio Vizintín.

1665
02:01:21.083 --> 02:01:22.916
<i>Antonio Vizintín.</i>

1666
02:01:24.291 --> 02:01:25.875
<i>Pedro Algorta.</i>

1667
02:01:26.625 --> 02:01:27.875
<i>Pedro Algorta.</i>

1668
02:01:28.375 --> 02:01:29.875
<i>Alfredo Delgado.</i>

1669
02:01:30.375 --> 02:01:31.791
<i>Alfredo Delgado.</i>

1670
02:01:32.333 --> 02:01:34.000
<i>Roy Harley.</i>

1671
02:01:34.500 --> 02:01:35.500
<i>Roy Harley.</i>

1672
02:01:36.375 --> 02:01:38.208
<i>José Luis Inciarte.</i>

1673
02:01:38.291 --> 02:01:39.583
<i>José Luis Inciarte.</i>

1674
02:01:40.625 --> 02:01:41.833
Ramón Sabella.

1675
02:01:42.958 --> 02:01:44.583
<i>Ramón Sabella.</i>

1676
02:01:45.083 --> 02:01:46.458
<i>Javier Methol.</i>

1677
02:01:47.166 --> 02:01:48.500
<i>Javier Methol.</i>

1678
02:01:50.125 --> 02:01:52.958
Carlitos Miguel Páez, my son.

1679
02:01:53.458 --> 02:01:56.625
<i>Carlitos Miguel Páez, my son.</i>

1680
02:01:58.833 --> 02:02:00.458
<i>Roberto François.</i>

1681
02:02:01.458 --> 02:02:03.541
<i>Roberto François.</i>

1682
02:02:03.625 --> 02:02:05.833
[helicopter blades whirring in distance]

1683
02:02:06.583 --> 02:02:08.166
[Páez] <i>Daniel Fernández.</i>

1684
02:02:08.666 --> 02:02:09.708
<i>Daniel Fernández.</i>

1685
02:02:11.500 --> 02:02:12.708
<i>Adolfo Strauch.</i>

1686
02:02:13.708 --> 02:02:15.208
<i>Adolfo Strauch.</i>

1687
02:02:16.250 --> 02:02:19.541
- [music swells]
- [all cheering]

1688
02:02:24.541 --> 02:02:25.666
[laughing]

1689
02:02:27.541 --> 02:02:29.125
There they are! There they are!

1690
02:02:29.208 --> 02:02:30.791
It's all of them!

1691
02:02:30.875 --> 02:02:32.541
All of them! Hey!

1692
02:02:32.625 --> 02:02:34.916
[laughing]

1693
02:02:36.208 --> 02:02:38.000
[crying]

1694
02:02:39.208 --> 02:02:40.708
[both laughing]

1695
02:02:41.708 --> 02:02:43.125
[camera clicks]

1696
02:02:53.041 --> 02:02:55.875
[shouting]

1697
02:02:55.958 --> 02:02:58.166
[laughing]

1698
02:03:01.250 --> 02:03:03.166
- Come on! Let's go!
- Whoo!

1699
02:03:03.250 --> 02:03:04.625
Let's go!

1700
02:03:05.833 --> 02:03:07.208
[cheering]

1701
02:03:09.916 --> 02:03:11.583
We're going home!

1702
02:03:24.333 --> 02:03:25.541
[both laugh]

1703
02:03:25.625 --> 02:03:28.041
Come on, Roy! Get up, man!

1704
02:03:33.583 --> 02:03:37.375
- [Fito] Come on, Gustavo!
- Hey! Leave it! Leave it!

1705
02:03:37.458 --> 02:03:40.166
- What do you mean?
- [soldier] Put it down!

1706
02:03:41.666 --> 02:03:43.166
Stop! Stop!

1707
02:03:43.250 --> 02:03:45.833
- Gustavo, let's go!
- No! I'm not going without the luggage!

1708
02:03:45.916 --> 02:03:48.041
- No!
- Get in! Get in! What are you doing?

1709
02:03:48.125 --> 02:03:49.958
Fine, bring it in.

1710
02:03:50.041 --> 02:03:51.750
- Bring it in!
- [soldier] Get in! Come on!

1711
02:03:51.833 --> 02:03:53.791
Come on! Let's go!

1712
02:03:54.458 --> 02:03:55.666
Come on!

1713
02:03:57.916 --> 02:03:59.375
[music swells]

1714
02:04:02.125 --> 02:04:04.125
[music fades]

1715
02:04:09.583 --> 02:04:13.083
[gentle instrumental music continues]

1716
02:04:25.000 --> 02:04:27.250
[fuselage creaking]

1717
02:04:54.125 --> 02:04:57.500
[Numa] <i>On December 22, 1972,</i>

1718
02:04:57.583 --> 02:05:01.375
<i>16 survivors came back
from the Andean Mountain Range.</i>

1719
02:05:04.125 --> 02:05:06.083
<i>Today my voice carries their words.</i>

1720
02:05:08.583 --> 02:05:10.958
<i>How each of us played our part.</i>

1721
02:05:11.041 --> 02:05:12.500
[laughing]

1722
02:05:13.500 --> 02:05:16.708
- [Numa] <i>This is our story.</i>
- [group laughing]

1723
02:05:24.083 --> 02:05:25.166
[Gustavo, in distance] Mom!

1724
02:05:25.250 --> 02:05:26.791
[laughing]

1725
02:05:31.833 --> 02:05:34.625
[mother gasping]

1726
02:05:34.708 --> 02:05:36.083
This is a miracle.

1727
02:05:37.291 --> 02:05:39.833
- This is a miracle.
- What miracle, Ma?

1728
02:05:39.916 --> 02:05:41.333
What miracle?

1729
02:05:45.666 --> 02:05:49.250
[crowd pounding on windows]

1730
02:05:49.333 --> 02:05:51.333
[all cheering and applauding]

1731
02:06:04.375 --> 02:06:06.833
[Numa] <i>The homecoming is overwhelming.</i>

1732
02:06:09.208 --> 02:06:10.958
<i>What is this crowd doing here?</i>

1733
02:06:14.458 --> 02:06:19.041
<i>They want to get close to my friends.
Touch them, know everything.</i>

1734
02:06:20.083 --> 02:06:21.958
<i>"What happened on the mountain?"</i>

1735
02:06:25.458 --> 02:06:28.000
We made it! Thank you!

1736
02:06:28.083 --> 02:06:29.458
Thank you!

1737
02:06:29.541 --> 02:06:33.208
[Numa] <i>Journalists want to know,
with their cameras and microphones.</i>

1738
02:06:33.291 --> 02:06:34.583
[flashlight clicks]

1739
02:06:36.750 --> 02:06:41.541
[Numa] <i>Doctors want to know,
with their exams and instruments.</i>

1740
02:06:47.541 --> 02:06:49.166
<i>What do they see?</i>

1741
02:06:55.625 --> 02:06:58.041
<i>They're scared of their dirty clothes.</i>

1742
02:07:00.916 --> 02:07:03.666
<i>Their skeletal bodies, baked by the sun.</i>

1743
02:07:09.291 --> 02:07:10.666
<i>The grime on their skin.</i>

1744
02:07:37.541 --> 02:07:38.791
[woman] Nando!

1745
02:07:40.958 --> 02:07:43.625
[Numa] <i>The newspapers talk
about the heroes of the Andes.</i>

1746
02:07:43.708 --> 02:07:46.583
[family crying]

1747
02:07:46.666 --> 02:07:50.291
[Numa] <i>The ones who came back from death
to reunite with their fathers...</i>

1748
02:07:53.583 --> 02:07:54.875
<i>Their mothers.</i>

1749
02:07:55.458 --> 02:07:58.625
- You look like an old man.
- [both laugh]

1750
02:08:00.416 --> 02:08:03.041
- [Roberto and girlfriend crying]
- [Numa] <i>Their girlfriends.</i>

1751
02:08:08.250 --> 02:08:10.666
- [family crying]
- [Numa] <i>And their children.</i>

1752
02:08:23.458 --> 02:08:25.458
[shuddering]

1753
02:08:33.125 --> 02:08:35.291
[Numa] <i>But they don't feel like heroes.</i>

1754
02:08:36.041 --> 02:08:37.958
[shower running]

1755
02:08:38.041 --> 02:08:42.500
[Numa] <i>Because they were dead like us,
and only they got to come back home.</i>

1756
02:08:42.583 --> 02:08:45.000
- [water dripping]
- [fuselage creaking]

1757
02:08:58.208 --> 02:09:00.583
[wind gusting]

1758
02:09:02.791 --> 02:09:04.791
[breeze blowing]

1759
02:09:08.083 --> 02:09:09.958
[Numa] <i>Now when they remember us,</i>

1760
02:09:10.833 --> 02:09:14.291
<i>they ask themselves,
"Why didn't we all get to come back?"</i>

1761
02:09:16.416 --> 02:09:17.875
<i>"What does it all mean?"</i>

1762
02:09:22.916 --> 02:09:24.958
<i>You'll need to find out yourselves.</i>

1763
02:09:29.083 --> 02:09:31.083
<i>'Cause the answer is in</i> you.

1764
02:09:40.375 --> 02:09:42.375
<i>Keep taking care of each other.</i>

1765
02:09:44.791 --> 02:09:47.541
<i>And tell everyone
what we did on the mountain.</i>

1766
02:09:54.041 --> 02:10:00.583
SOCIETY OF THE SNOW

1767
02:10:03.750 --> 02:10:05.750
[gentle orchestral music continues]

1768
02:10:28.125 --> 02:10:31.166
BASED ON SOCIETY OF THE SNOW
BY PABLO VIERCI

1769
02:11:56.625 --> 02:11:59.083
{\an8}[uplifting vocals]

1770
02:12:57.916 --> 02:13:00.708
[gentle music fades]

1771
02:13:00.791 --> 02:13:02.791
{\an8}[energetic string music playing]

1772
02:13:44.458 --> 02:13:46.458
{\an8}[rhythmic clapping]

1773
02:15:16.000 --> 02:15:18.625
[tense, rhythmic music playing]

1774
02:18:31.041 --> 02:18:33.041
[menacing, rhythmic music playing]

1775
02:19:11.500 --> 02:19:13.500
[bright instrumental music playing]

1776
02:19:52.833 --> 02:19:54.833
[gentle, uplifting vocals]

1777
02:21:03.708 --> 02:21:07.333
[music builds to a powerful crescendo]

1778
02:22:46.500 --> 02:22:51.333
Subtitle translation by: Meredith Cannella

1779
02:23:03.083 --> 02:23:06.458
[music fades slowly]
